WEBVTT

00:18.010 --> 00:20.770
The world is amidst the Great Pirate Era.

00:21.060 --> 00:26.550
In pursuit of fame, fortune and power,
ambitious souls take to the sea.

00:27.190 --> 00:30.740
For pirates, it's an era that is like a dream.

00:31.240 --> 00:36.200
But among them, there are those
who seek only to plunder...

00:36.700 --> 00:43.280
And for the powerless, it means
an age of relentless oppression.

00:44.000 --> 00:49.750
Even the Navy, working at the behest of the
World Government, can not help everyone...

00:50.800 --> 00:54.010
So who can the oppressed turn to?

00:54.510 --> 00:57.720
On what can they pin
their hopes for salvation?

00:58.720 --> 01:00.390
We're in a real fix...

01:00.510 --> 01:04.020
No one's looking out for folks like us.

01:05.060 --> 01:07.900
I cry all the time lately...

01:09.060 --> 01:12.780
Everyone agrees:
the Navy is bad, but what's worse is...

01:12.900 --> 01:14.990
I'm hungry!

01:15.110 --> 01:18.490
What did you expect?
The pirates took everything.

01:18.620 --> 01:20.120
That's right! It's the pirates' fault!

01:20.240 --> 01:21.950
Because of them being so greedy...

01:22.080 --> 01:24.080
No one gets to have fun anymore!

01:27.460 --> 01:29.290
Do you understand what we're going through?

01:29.920 --> 01:32.550
Please. We're suffering...

01:33.170 --> 01:35.840
You're the only one.
The only one who can help...!

01:36.010 --> 01:37.720
--You can fix this...

01:36.010 --> 01:37.720
--Please.

01:37.840 --> 01:39.890
--You're only only hope!

01:37.840 --> 01:39.890
--I'm begging you.

01:40.010 --> 01:40.930
Please!

01:42.060 --> 01:44.980
I know. I know, everyone.

01:45.480 --> 01:50.730
I'm going to create a new age
where you can all be happy.

02:15.300 --> 02:17.630
This is one huge crowd.

02:17.760 --> 02:21.220
Well, the famous Uta is performing live
in front of a crowd for the first time!

02:21.550 --> 02:25.350
She's only done stuff over Video
Transponder Snails until now!

02:25.720 --> 02:30.150
Uta in person!
And in such an awesome place!

02:30.270 --> 02:32.650
I'm... I'm so...!

02:35.860 --> 02:39.410
There's even merfolk around.
Should be quite a show.

02:39.530 --> 02:41.910
But why are we dressed like this?

02:42.030 --> 02:46.750
Showing up in costume to help hype up
her first show gets you these!

02:46.870 --> 02:48.210
That's why?

02:48.330 --> 02:49.830
I'm looking forward to it.

02:50.040 --> 02:52.840
She's the entire world's
sweetheart, at this point.

02:52.960 --> 02:54.920
Is this chick really that big a deal?

02:55.130 --> 02:59.840
As odd as it might sound coming from
Soul King, her voice is otherworldly.

03:00.050 --> 03:03.800
U! T! A! Uta-chan!

03:03.930 --> 03:04.990
What a loser.

03:06.060 --> 03:10.390
Hey, shitty swordsman! Say that again
and I'll cook you up nice and juicy!

03:10.520 --> 03:12.610
I'd like to see you try, Twirly Brow.

03:15.130 --> 03:16.940
Here we go!

03:17.320 --> 03:20.320
Hey! The show's starting, Luffy!

03:22.700 --> 03:26.580
<i>♪We can choose the way of our future♪</i>

03:26.700 --> 03:33.710
<i>♪Try a brand new path...
If I change the world</i>♪

03:34.630 --> 03:42.300
<i>♪If I change the world</i>♪

04:06.240 --> 04:08.790
<i>♪Say goodbye to everyone
who stands against us</i>♪

04:09.040 --> 04:13.000
<i>♪No one has the power to stop a change
that comes through music</i>♪

04:13.450 --> 04:15.820
<i>♪No, you can't stop magic</i>♪

04:17.250 --> 04:19.880
<i>♪Close your eyes and you can see
the future before you</i>♪

04:20.010 --> 04:23.630
<i>♪Every note I sing is bringin' you
closer to your purpose♪</i>

04:24.470 --> 04:28.310
<i>♪Once you're there don't let go</i>♪

04:28.560 --> 04:30.980
<i>♪You wanna play a real game,
unfurl the chain</i>♪

04:31.100 --> 04:33.940
<i>♪Melody strung out like we're
walkin' on a tight rope</i>♪

04:34.060 --> 04:36.440
<i>♪Don't wanna cry,
don't wanna try, wanna forget</i>♪

04:36.560 --> 04:40.940
<i>♪Just let me live inside a dreamland
Wanna be free!</i>♪

04:41.070 --> 04:46.370
<i>♪And let a brand new era dawn</i>♪

04:46.490 --> 04:49.160
<i>♪I know that we can
Create a new world!♪</i>

04:50.290 --> 04:52.830
<i>♪We can choose the way of our future♪</i>

04:52.960 --> 04:57.420
<i>♪Try a brand new path...
If I change the world♪</i>

04:57.540 --> 05:00.670
<i>♪If I change the world...♪</i>

05:01.170 --> 05:05.510
<i>♪This boundless music brings transformation
Messages in song</i>♪

05:05.720 --> 05:11.180
<i>♪Reach even further
This dream will come true♪</i>

05:11.210 --> 05:12.720
<i>♪I believe in you♪</i>

05:34.080 --> 05:36.710
<i>♪Say goodbye to everything
that's weighing you down♪</i>

05:36.830 --> 05:40.660
<i>♪Transcend beyond reality
to colorful worlds of music♪</i>

05:41.190 --> 05:43.290
<i>♪We need to keep on rising♪</i>

05:45.010 --> 05:47.630
<i>♪Close your eyes and take my hand
we're runnin' together♪</i>

05:47.760 --> 05:51.470
<i>♪We don't have to live like this,
I know we can all do better♪</i>

05:52.260 --> 05:56.190
<i>♪I sing for liberation♪</i>

05:56.390 --> 05:58.770
<i>♪You wanna play a real game,
unfurl the chain♪</i>

05:58.900 --> 06:01.650
<i>♪Melody lighting up the path to new horizons♪</i>

06:01.820 --> 06:04.400
<i>♪Don't wanna cry,
don't wanna try, wanna forget♪</i>

06:04.530 --> 06:08.700
<i>♪Just let me live inside a dreamland
Wanna be free!♪</i>

06:08.910 --> 06:14.200
<i>♪And let a brand new era dawn♪</i>

06:14.330 --> 06:16.540
<i>♪I know that we can
Create a new world!♪</i>

06:18.080 --> 06:20.580
<i>♪We can choose the way of our future♪</i>

06:20.710 --> 06:25.210
<i>♪Try a brand new path
If I change the world...♪</i>

06:25.340 --> 06:28.430
<i>♪If I change the world...♪</i>

06:28.930 --> 06:33.510
<i>♪This boundless music brings transformation
Messages in song♪</i>

06:33.640 --> 06:36.370
<i>♪Reach even further♪</i>

06:36.390 --> 06:39.020
<i>♪Reach even further♪</i>

06:39.020 --> 06:41.020
<i>♪A New Genesis♪</i>

07:00.870 --> 07:02.420
<i>♪A New Genesis♪</i>

07:14.560 --> 07:17.930
It's great to finally meet you all! I'm Uta!

07:23.560 --> 07:25.940
Sorry... this is a lot to take in.

07:35.910 --> 07:39.000
Let's all have a great time today!

07:40.620 --> 07:42.740
You boys ready?

07:42.740 --> 07:43.750
Yeah.

07:43.750 --> 07:48.670
Snatch up a star like her
and we'll be rich and famous!

07:49.090 --> 07:51.380
Too bad for you, Uta!

07:51.510 --> 07:55.220
U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A!

07:58.390 --> 07:59.390
Whoa, Luffy!

08:03.900 --> 08:06.770
Is this guy after Uta, too?

08:08.190 --> 08:10.240
Hey, I was right!

08:11.280 --> 08:13.160
Uta! You're Uta, aren't you?!

08:13.280 --> 08:15.370
It's me, remember?!

08:15.570 --> 08:16.530
Me?

08:17.120 --> 08:19.950
Wait... Luffy?!

08:20.080 --> 08:22.370
It's been a real long time, Uta!

08:22.580 --> 08:25.000
Luffy!

08:25.130 --> 08:26.570
Wha--?!

08:37.970 --> 08:40.600
--It can't be!

08:37.970 --> 08:40.600
--Wait, that straw hat...

08:40.600 --> 08:40.820
--It can't be!

08:40.600 --> 08:40.820
--The fifth Emperor?!

08:40.830 --> 08:44.270
No way. Uta wouldn't be friends with a pirate!

08:46.360 --> 08:48.650
Luffy knows Uta?

08:48.770 --> 08:51.240
Dammit! He could've introduced us, then!

08:51.360 --> 08:53.650
Why exactly are you so friendly
with Princess Uta--?

08:53.780 --> 08:54.990
Huh?!

08:55.110 --> 08:57.700
'Cause she's Shanks' daughter!

09:07.880 --> 09:09.210
When he says Shanks...

09:09.340 --> 09:11.880
That's one of the Four Emperors.
A major bad guy!

09:12.010 --> 09:13.220
I remember a long time ago...

09:13.340 --> 09:16.680
Yeah. He's the one who attacked Elegia!

09:18.390 --> 09:19.390
Uta...

09:23.140 --> 09:27.100
I had thought it was odd
that Elegia was the venue...

09:27.230 --> 09:29.110
Because of the old legend?

09:29.230 --> 09:32.900
Right. But this adds a whole new wrinkle to it.

09:37.200 --> 09:38.240
Who're you guys?

09:38.370 --> 09:41.700
So "Red-Haired" Shanks of the Four
Emperors has a daughter?

09:41.830 --> 09:45.160
If it's true, that'd make you
his biggest weakness...

09:45.290 --> 09:46.580
Red-Haired's baby girl!

09:46.710 --> 09:50.790
We fork you over to one the big-name
pirate crews and we'll make a huge profit!

09:50.920 --> 09:55.130
So there you have it.
Sorry, but this concert is canceled!

09:55.550 --> 09:57.550
Heat Beating!

10:02.140 --> 10:04.430
We'll be taking the girl!

10:04.730 --> 10:05.850
It's you...

10:05.980 --> 10:07.060
--Branch?

10:07.190 --> 10:10.150
My name is Brulee! With the Big Mom Pirates!

10:10.270 --> 10:11.480
What about the other guy?

10:11.610 --> 10:15.240
I'm Big Mom a.k.a Charlotte
Linlin's fourth son, Oven.

10:15.360 --> 10:17.820
This looks like fun. I want in!

10:17.950 --> 10:22.700
Seriously! I was curious about the fuss
and got lucky enough to hear the big reveal!

10:23.660 --> 10:27.290
Sorry, Uta, but you're going
to be my gift to Mama!

10:27.970 --> 10:28.650
Hang on.

10:29.640 --> 10:30.400
It'll be okay.

10:30.920 --> 10:31.890
Whoa, woah!

10:31.890 --> 10:35.420
If any of you scumbags are after Uta-chan,
you'll have to go through me!

10:35.550 --> 10:39.760
I can hardly ignore the kind of rogues who
would interrupt such a stirring performance.

10:39.890 --> 10:42.930
Now this is my idea of entertainment!

10:43.060 --> 10:46.680
Don't mess with the Jellyfish Pirates!

10:47.020 --> 10:49.640
Song of Scratches... Blizzard Slice!

10:51.690 --> 10:53.150
Kraken Fist!

10:56.190 --> 10:57.070
I guess we're doing this!

10:57.190 --> 10:59.570
The show's just getting started!

10:59.700 --> 11:02.450
Let's get it on! We're gonna protect Uta!

11:02.570 --> 11:06.580
Fishman Karate! Spear Wave!

11:09.620 --> 11:12.830
I can super take it from here!

11:16.250 --> 11:20.180
Gum-Gum... Jet Gatling!

11:22.680 --> 11:25.560
Cien Fleurs! Spider Net!

11:26.350 --> 11:27.520
Alrighty!

11:27.930 --> 11:29.430
Okay! That's enough!

11:29.560 --> 11:34.020
Luffy, guys, thanks for protecting me!
But no more brawling!

11:34.150 --> 11:35.150
You think this is just a brawl?!

11:35.320 --> 11:39.070
You're all my fans, so I want you all
enjoying the show and getting along!

11:39.900 --> 11:43.700
But these guys are trying
to kidnap you, Princess Uta!

11:43.820 --> 11:46.740
And they don't seem like the reasonable type!

11:46.870 --> 11:50.080
When we want something, we fight to take it!

11:50.210 --> 11:51.920
Because we're pirates!

11:52.040 --> 11:53.880
So stop being pirates, then.

11:54.000 --> 11:57.130
I'll forgive all the bad stuff
you've done until now.

11:57.250 --> 12:00.760
Why don't all of you give up
this nasty pirate business

12:00.880 --> 12:04.470
and join me in a world
with tons of fun instead?

12:05.640 --> 12:09.390
With my songs, we can all
be happy and enjoy peace!

12:12.020 --> 12:14.350
There's no such thing as peace, girl.

12:14.480 --> 12:17.480
If you wanna keep yapping,
I can slice your face up!

12:17.610 --> 12:20.400
Hang on! She belongs to me.

12:20.530 --> 12:22.240
--It's fine.

12:20.530 --> 12:22.240
--Uta!

12:22.780 --> 12:25.620
Come on, I thought you all came
here to enjoy my singing.

12:26.570 --> 12:30.580
We're pirates, baby. There's stuff that
matters to us more than music!

12:31.040 --> 12:31.960
This is awful!

12:32.110 --> 12:33.580
They're ruining the concert...

12:33.590 --> 12:36.040
They don't care how Uta or any of us feel.

12:36.500 --> 12:37.790
What a shame.

12:38.130 --> 12:40.050
In that case, I'll make a song out of you.

12:46.300 --> 12:52.810
<i>♪Now, let worry fall away
No fear allowed to stay♪</i>

12:53.020 --> 12:57.900
<i>♪My dream is now your wish
And my hope is never-ending♪</i>

12:58.060 --> 13:02.860
<i>♪When clouds build up inside
My song can clear the sky♪</i>

13:03.070 --> 13:08.990
<i>♪You know I'm invincible
Everything is alright♪</i>

13:17.040 --> 13:21.960
<i>♪My voice carries birds in flight
With ev'ry note, they go higher and higher♪</i>

13:22.090 --> 13:26.930
<i>♪See how I move with such grace
Just like a dancer on the stage♪</i>

13:27.140 --> 13:32.180
<i>♪Your voice carries life within
Calls me to action again and again♪</i>

13:32.470 --> 13:34.980
<i>♪If you're hurt and you need
I'll always be there, I swear♪</i>

13:35.100 --> 13:37.100
<i>♪I'll always protect you♪</i>

13:37.230 --> 13:41.860
<i>♪We'll have the chance to go
to brand new heights♪</i>

13:41.980 --> 13:46.660
<i>♪You and I, unstoppable when we're together
We can have it all♪</i>

13:46.990 --> 13:49.200
<i>♪A fire burns within in our hearts♪</i>

13:49.530 --> 13:55.410
<i>♪Now, let's go hand in hand
To a light that lies ahead♪</i>

13:55.540 --> 13:59.500
<i>♪All of hopes and dreams
Can bring happiness when we're in sync♪</i>

13:59.630 --> 14:05.340
<i>♪I've always felt this warmth from you
No one gives affection like you do♪</i>

14:05.470 --> 14:11.640
<i>♪You make me invincible
When you're here by my side♪</i>

14:12.760 --> 14:18.100
<i>♪Strong with you by my side♪</i>

14:20.980 --> 14:25.280
Okay, guys, those bad pirates
are now part of a fun song!

14:25.400 --> 14:28.070
Everything should be fine now, so you can relax!

14:33.160 --> 14:37.290
That's right! They might be family,
but Uta is nothing like Shanks!

14:37.410 --> 14:38.790
Thank goodness!

14:38.920 --> 14:41.500
You're real strong now, Uta!

14:50.010 --> 14:52.350
She's gotta have some kind of power, right?

14:52.470 --> 14:54.640
Not that I'm aware of, but maybe...

14:54.760 --> 14:56.680
What the heck is this?

14:56.810 --> 14:59.390
What're you doing? Let's get back to our seats!

15:02.150 --> 15:04.980
Now, I've got some great news
to share with you all!

15:06.650 --> 15:12.040
I would always get tired during the streaming
concerts with Video Transponder Snails,

15:12.060 --> 15:13.490
so they tended to be pretty short...

15:13.780 --> 15:17.290
But this concert is an endless one!
It's gonna keep going, non-stop!

15:18.250 --> 15:21.670
That's right! We can be together, forever!

15:21.960 --> 15:26.170
Everybody watching the broadcast
and everyone here at the venue!

15:26.300 --> 15:28.090
Let's all keep having a great time!

15:32.180 --> 15:35.970
This is crazy! She's gonna do
a non-stop solo show?!

15:36.100 --> 15:37.270
How cool is that?!

15:37.720 --> 15:42.110
U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A!

15:42.120 --> 15:48.530
U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A...!

15:48.650 --> 15:51.150
And there's one other thing I need to say.

15:51.450 --> 15:55.530
To all you pirates, the Navy,
and to the people at the World Government.

15:55.660 --> 15:57.370
do not try to stop this concert.

15:57.910 --> 16:01.460
Everyone is looking for fun
and things to make them happy.

16:01.580 --> 16:04.330
If you ruin that... there'll be consequences.

16:04.670 --> 16:07.590
I'm Uta, the woman who's
going to create a new age.

16:07.750 --> 16:09.800
And I'm going to use my songs
to make everyone happy!

16:12.430 --> 16:15.260
Okay, let's move to the next number.

16:18.490 --> 16:28.300
"Highest Authorities of the World Government"
"The Five Elders"

16:18.600 --> 16:20.680
Red-Haired had a Daughter all along, eh?

16:20.810 --> 16:23.230
Cipher Pol's report was accurate.

16:23.350 --> 16:28.230
This is a new threat, one that's
opposed to the Great Pirate Era.

16:28.360 --> 16:32.280
The real problem is how she has popular support.

16:32.400 --> 16:36.070
We should end any seeds of
rebellion before it's too late.

16:36.200 --> 16:39.910
Even if this girl is of Figarland Blood?

16:40.370 --> 16:43.750
I'm concerned about the presence
of Tot Musica as well.

16:44.210 --> 16:45.920
Tot Musica...

16:46.170 --> 16:51.720
With the threat it poses if awoken,
we can't afford to be cautious.

16:54.470 --> 16:57.720
Yeah. The order to subdue Uta has just come in.

16:57.850 --> 16:59.140
She's too damn dangerous.

16:59.260 --> 17:05.100
It's funny enough that a single girl
has the whole world's attention.

17:05.520 --> 17:07.730
Hey! You better not take her lightly!

17:08.190 --> 17:10.730
The target's on the island of Music, Elegia.

17:10.860 --> 17:14.820
The same spot where Tot Musica
was sealed away in ancient times.

17:15.030 --> 17:17.280
And what kind of numbers are we sending?

17:17.660 --> 17:20.790
How many ships are ready to set sail for Elegia?

17:21.120 --> 17:22.370
Thirty.

17:22.500 --> 17:26.330
Good! Send them all,
loaded for bear with troops!

17:27.670 --> 17:28.770
--In the event of Transponder Snail interference,
orders from the flagship will be issued

17:28.770 --> 17:31.630
--Code has been issued to crews already and orders
are to prepare response flags immediately.

17:31.630 --> 17:39.350
--using the flag signals notated under
Code 044 in the Signal Book...

17:48.980 --> 17:52.280
Okay, are any of you hungry?

17:52.820 --> 17:57.320
In that case, I'm gonna make plenty
of food and other stuff to enjoy!

18:00.460 --> 18:02.290
Can I really keep it?

18:02.410 --> 18:03.580
Of course!

18:03.700 --> 18:06.870
I want you all to eat whenever you want,
wherever you want!

18:07.000 --> 18:11.380
Sing and dance with me and have a good time!

18:11.630 --> 18:12.960
It's like a dream...

18:13.250 --> 18:16.340
Stick with me and all your
dreams will come true!

18:16.470 --> 18:19.680
There's nothing to scare us anywhere!

18:19.890 --> 18:22.220
This new age is the greatest!

18:29.230 --> 18:34.230
Her power's even greater than expected!
I suppose we've underestimated her.

18:36.650 --> 18:43.700
And on top of that, she's Red-Haired's daughter?
I want her, no matter what it takes.

18:43.830 --> 18:47.410
Those pain-in-the-neck Straw
hats are with her, too!

18:47.540 --> 18:50.040
I'd like to see them try and take me on. Lick!

18:50.330 --> 18:52.090
I'll go to Elegia.

18:54.750 --> 18:58.800
I'm not going to stay quiet
when she's captured my sister.

19:02.010 --> 19:04.310
This place is a real chef's paradise.

19:04.430 --> 19:06.560
I asked Uta for booze and she whipped it up.

19:06.680 --> 19:10.060
I know! I bet we could ask her
to create all kinds of treasure.

19:10.190 --> 19:12.230
How do you think her powers work?

19:12.440 --> 19:14.650
--Woah, there...
--She's a little too versatile

19:14.650 --> 19:16.080
to have just eaten a Devil Fruit.

19:16.320 --> 19:17.780
You've got a point.

19:17.900 --> 19:20.360
I've never heard of powers
capable to be doing all this.

19:20.490 --> 19:24.160
Luffy, you're friends with Uta, right?
Do you know anything?

19:24.450 --> 19:28.200
She always really loved singing!

19:28.830 --> 19:29.170
Huh?

19:31.170 --> 19:38.210
Perhaps Uta has been gifted with
almighty powers from the gods of music!

19:38.340 --> 19:40.550
Luffy. Guys. You having fun?

19:40.680 --> 19:42.470
Yes, Princess Uta!

19:42.590 --> 19:45.510
With all these unusual ingredients?
This place is heaven!

19:45.810 --> 19:47.930
There's so much fun stuff!

19:48.060 --> 19:51.520
I'm glad I could make Luffy's friends happy.

19:52.310 --> 19:54.340
--Hey, is this everybody?
--Yep.

19:54.530 --> 19:56.700
That can't be right. That hat belongs to--

19:56.830 --> 19:57.920
This is everybody!

19:59.690 --> 20:01.860
It's been a while, Luffy,
so how about another game?

20:01.990 --> 20:04.620
There's no way you can beat me now.

20:04.740 --> 20:08.580
What are you talking about?
I'm on a 183-game-long winning streak!

20:08.750 --> 20:11.920
Wrong! I won those 183 times!

20:12.210 --> 20:14.210
Those are extremely divergent perspectives.

20:14.330 --> 20:15.630
What kind of game?

20:16.040 --> 20:20.970
Luffy and I used to compete all the time.
At knife throwing, arm wrestling...

20:21.300 --> 20:24.260
Okay! This is what we're gonna do today!

20:29.890 --> 20:30.850
Whoa!

20:31.810 --> 20:34.690
It's a game of chicken!
Whoever eats fastest wins.

20:34.980 --> 20:37.900
Oh, I remember this! That just leaves...

20:38.020 --> 20:40.610
Don't worry. I've got it covered!

20:43.490 --> 20:44.990
--Ready...

20:43.490 --> 20:44.990
--Let's do this!

20:45.110 --> 20:46.620
Three, two, one, go!

20:58.750 --> 20:59.260
For you.

21:00.360 --> 21:01.540
Thanks!

21:06.800 --> 21:08.140
Uta won!

21:08.150 --> 21:09.550
She wins!

21:09.680 --> 21:11.560
That was cheap, Uta!

21:13.690 --> 21:14.810
Aw, crap, right into the ocean.

21:22.650 --> 21:26.660
Oh, right! You ate a Devil Fruit, too,
huh, Luffy? Sorry about that!

21:26.780 --> 21:29.240
You cheated back there! I want a do-over!

21:29.370 --> 21:31.120
There you go again, being a sore loser!

21:31.450 --> 21:34.940
And since I won, you better
tell me where Shanks is!

21:34.950 --> 21:35.540
I dunno.

21:35.670 --> 21:38.070
Then why've you got his straw hat?

21:38.300 --> 21:38.960
He let me borrow it.

21:39.000 --> 21:42.260
Hey, question!
Where did you two meet, anyway?

21:42.550 --> 21:47.050
She came to Fusha Village
along with Shanks and his crew!

21:47.180 --> 21:50.010
That's your hometown, isn't it?

21:50.260 --> 21:51.310
Yeah!

21:52.040 --> 21:55.160
12 years ago.

21:57.810 --> 21:59.900
Uta's daydreaming again!

22:00.980 --> 22:02.110
You should come up here.

22:02.360 --> 22:03.390
No way! Boring!

22:03.820 --> 22:05.460
I wanna play a game instead!

22:05.700 --> 22:08.280
Honestly, you're such a baby.

22:08.610 --> 22:10.740
In that case, how about...

22:11.080 --> 22:12.490
A game of chicken!

22:14.200 --> 22:16.370
Winner eats the most then runs away.

22:16.500 --> 22:17.330
Yeah!

22:17.460 --> 22:20.290
That's dangerous! Cut that out, you two.

22:20.420 --> 22:21.040
No way!

22:21.110 --> 22:22.440
Uta! Luffy!

22:22.630 --> 22:24.840
Let them have their fun.

22:26.720 --> 22:29.510
This is their idea of serious competition.

22:30.760 --> 22:32.310
--Let's do it!
--Ready...

22:32.430 --> 22:33.560
Three, two, one, go!

22:35.140 --> 22:37.270
What are they competing over, anyway?

22:37.390 --> 22:40.100
Who's going to become
the bigger pirate, apparently.

22:43.940 --> 22:45.490
Is Luffy gonna win?

22:46.400 --> 22:47.360
Here's some juice.

22:47.920 --> 22:48.700
Thanks!

22:51.280 --> 22:52.200
Luffy!

22:52.330 --> 22:54.790
I can't believe he fell for it again!

22:55.040 --> 22:56.120
You okay?

22:56.250 --> 22:59.210
It's not over!
That didn't settle nothing!

22:59.330 --> 23:00.960
You're being a sore loser again!

23:01.080 --> 23:02.590
Well, you cheated, so you lose!

23:02.790 --> 23:05.460
I'm a pirate! There's no such thing as cheating!

23:05.590 --> 23:08.550
You got careless in a duel
because you're a dumb baby!

23:08.670 --> 23:12.550
It's not like Shanks says
you're a real pirate yet!

23:12.680 --> 23:15.430
Shut up! I'm Shanks' daughter!

23:15.560 --> 23:19.350
Unlike you, I've been sailing and going
on adventures for years now!

23:19.480 --> 23:21.230
That's a huge difference!

23:21.350 --> 23:22.400
--Is not!
--Is, too!

23:22.520 --> 23:25.230
In that case, let's fight to
settle it--like real pirates!

23:25.360 --> 23:26.860
Fine with me!

23:33.050 --> 23:35.120
Give it a rest already.

23:35.240 --> 23:39.460
No real pirate would use
their sword on a kid, Shanks!

23:39.580 --> 23:42.170
Don't be silly, that was just tough love.

23:42.420 --> 23:44.540
But swords are sharp, not tough!

23:44.790 --> 23:49.920
Aw, did you say love?
Does that mean you love me, Shanks?

23:50.050 --> 23:52.840
Shanks!

23:52.970 --> 23:56.140
Uta, Luffy, both of you need
to stop clinging to me!

23:56.430 --> 23:59.640
How come you call your dad "Shanks," anyway?

24:00.390 --> 24:03.560
He might be my dad, but he's also
my captain, and I idolize him!

24:03.690 --> 24:05.230
Isn't he cool?

24:07.440 --> 24:11.860
I'm feeling so good about beating
Luffy again, I think I'll sing!

24:11.990 --> 24:14.370
Shanks, I wanna go sailing, too!

24:14.620 --> 24:17.200
You're too rowdy for my crew.

24:17.330 --> 24:18.160
What about Uta?!

24:18.290 --> 24:22.000
She waits on the ship during battle.
There's no way you could sit still.

24:24.460 --> 24:28.420
That's right! I'm the Red-Haired
Pirates' musician, Uta!

24:28.550 --> 24:32.880
The girl who's gonna use music to make
a new age where everyone will be free!

24:33.010 --> 24:35.720
Pay attention, our musician's taking the stage.

24:41.930 --> 24:48.690
<i>♪Where did it come from
Where could this wind be taking us?</i>♪

24:49.280 --> 24:55.110
<i>♪I look up to the sky hoping for answers
But there is no reply</i>♪

24:55.660 --> 25:02.620
<i>♪Where will it end up,
The song that I've been a vessel for?♪</i>

25:03.040 --> 25:08.960
<i>♪I look within knowing I'll find the answer
Even on my own♪</i>

25:09.840 --> 25:15.550
<i>♪Let's row out to the open sea
far as we can go</i>♪

25:16.220 --> 25:18.850
<i>♪To the unknown</i>♪

25:21.390 --> 25:24.230
<i>♪I've got to keep--</i>

25:39.080 --> 25:40.660
Okay, I get to sing next!

25:40.790 --> 25:42.200
All right, let's hear it!

25:46.250 --> 25:49.250
Come to think of it,
you disappeared all of a sudden.

25:51.090 --> 25:53.170
It was sudden? How come?

25:53.630 --> 25:56.050
Let's see... If I can remember right...

25:57.430 --> 26:01.350
I used to wait for Shanks
and his crew to come back.

26:01.600 --> 26:02.970
But one time...

26:03.560 --> 26:04.770
Welcome back!

26:04.980 --> 26:07.340
What kinda adventures did you have this time?

26:07.900 --> 26:09.770
Huh? What's wrong?

26:10.190 --> 26:12.360
Fine, I'll just ask Uta!

26:12.480 --> 26:15.280
Uta! Uta!

26:15.610 --> 26:18.320
I'll listen to you brag about
your adventures again!

26:18.450 --> 26:20.200
Where are you, Uta?!

26:22.370 --> 26:25.250
Shanks? Where'd Uta go?

26:28.620 --> 26:32.130
Did... something happen to her?

26:33.300 --> 26:35.210
Don't worry, Luffy.

26:35.550 --> 26:40.680
Uta left the crew to become
a singer. That's all.

26:44.060 --> 26:47.480
So why'd you stop wanting to be a pirate, Uta?

26:47.600 --> 26:50.560
You used to love the Red-Haired Pirates so much!

26:52.060 --> 26:55.190
I wanted to be a singer more than a pirate.

26:55.320 --> 26:59.990
I mean, I've already got fans all over
the world after only two years!

27:01.450 --> 27:03.990
What about you, Luffy? What are you doing now?

27:04.120 --> 27:06.040
Are you joking? I'm a pirate!

27:08.080 --> 27:10.120
Right... You're a pirate, huh?

27:10.370 --> 27:13.090
Yeah! And I'm gonna be the King of the Pirates.

27:13.290 --> 27:16.090
Hey, Luffy... You should quit being a pirate.

27:17.240 --> 27:19.380
Why don't you live here, with us, and have fun?

27:19.550 --> 27:24.510
Your friends are all fans of mine, right?
It'd be way better to stay here.

27:24.720 --> 27:27.350
Hey! Are you listening, Luffy?

27:28.810 --> 27:31.600
It was great seeing you again, Uta!

27:31.730 --> 27:34.650
I ate some meat, so I'm gonna head
back to the Sunny and sleep.

27:35.690 --> 27:38.820
Looks like you're doing what
you want, and that's good!

27:38.940 --> 27:39.700
See ya!

27:40.030 --> 27:41.360
I'm not letting you go.

27:42.700 --> 27:46.430
All of you, and Luffy,
are staying here forever...

27:46.760 --> 27:48.500
Where you're going to have fun, with me.

27:48.620 --> 27:50.370
What the hell are you talking about?

27:50.500 --> 27:54.290
Uta, I love your singing,
but <i>forever</i> is a little--

27:55.380 --> 27:56.710
Nami-san!

27:57.000 --> 28:00.550
Everyone! I found more pirates!

28:00.720 --> 28:01.760
What should I do?

28:04.050 --> 28:05.600
U-T-A!

28:05.720 --> 28:08.680
U-T-A!

28:09.020 --> 28:12.560
U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A! U-T-A!

28:13.150 --> 28:14.270
Okay!

28:14.400 --> 28:17.980
I'll take care of the pirates for you, then!

28:29.620 --> 28:34.460
I don't care if you know Luffy,
you're having a little too much fun.

28:38.130 --> 28:39.670
What are these guys?!

28:41.090 --> 28:42.630
There are more and more of them!

28:42.840 --> 28:45.590
Arabesque Brick Fist!

28:49.010 --> 28:51.230
Ouchie Finger!

28:53.230 --> 28:54.230
Luffy...

28:54.940 --> 28:57.610
This is your fault for being a pirate.

28:57.730 --> 29:00.610
If you're really my friend,
then give up on being a pirate.

29:00.900 --> 29:02.290
What are you talking about?!

29:05.070 --> 29:07.280
I'm not doing this. Don't feel like it.

29:07.950 --> 29:09.790
There's no reason for us to fight.

29:10.160 --> 29:12.910
You might not want a fight, but I do!

29:31.180 --> 29:33.560
Seis Fleurs! Slap!

29:38.190 --> 29:40.610
Quit messing around, Uta!

29:41.610 --> 29:46.820
<i>♪My memories so good and awful
It seems they gave me a grudge♪</i>

29:48.030 --> 29:52.660
<i>♪But I have left bitterness
and resentment behind me♪</i>

29:53.040 --> 29:54.620
<i>♪And it is all thanks to him♪</i>

29:54.750 --> 29:56.210
<i>♪Look, it's the clowns who think they know♪</i>

29:56.330 --> 29:57.830
<i>♪How crushing loneliness can be♪</i>

29:57.960 --> 30:00.290
<i>♪You know nothing 'til you come with me♪</i>

30:00.420 --> 30:02.460
<i>♪And run wild!
Release your rage♪</i>

30:02.590 --> 30:07.260
<i>♪Let the winds of wrath blow them away♪</i>

30:07.380 --> 30:10.640
<i>♪Not gonna live in compliance-iance-iance♪</i>

30:10.760 --> 30:12.890
<i>♪I'm not playin' the victim, no more♪</i>

30:13.180 --> 30:18.020
<i>♪Time to go rage
Let's punish them all♪</i>

30:18.150 --> 30:20.440
<i>♪For their love; I'm done trying to trust♪</i>

30:20.560 --> 30:23.730
<i>♪Not gonna live in compliance-iance-iance♪</i>

30:23.860 --> 30:26.400
<i>♪Gonna play with fire, backlit♪</i>

30:26.530 --> 30:32.740
<i>♪By the flames♪</i>

30:43.250 --> 30:46.840
What the heck are you doing? Let me go!

30:47.050 --> 30:50.300
I can't... let you become the Pirate King.

30:52.680 --> 30:55.640
What do you all think of pirates?

30:56.270 --> 30:58.350
Pirates burnt my city down!

30:59.020 --> 31:01.310
Pirates killed my husband!

31:01.940 --> 31:03.480
Give my mom back!

31:03.610 --> 31:08.570
No more pirates! Throw them out!
No more pirates! Throw them out!

31:08.780 --> 31:12.870
Princess Uta! Luffy would never do that!

31:13.240 --> 31:15.240
Uta, let my crew go--!

31:17.540 --> 31:19.750
Stay away from Uta! Dammed pirate!

31:21.710 --> 31:24.840
Those Devil Fruit powers aren't scary
when you're weakened from seawater!

31:25.050 --> 31:26.510
Hey, stop it!

31:26.630 --> 31:27.530
I can't stand this--

31:27.600 --> 31:28.040
Don't.

31:28.510 --> 31:32.050
It'll be okay. We need to get
ready for the the next phase.

31:32.340 --> 31:34.180
Barrier Ball!

31:36.310 --> 31:38.310
L-Lomeo...?

31:38.430 --> 31:41.190
Luffy-senpai, there's something
real nasty about Uta-sama!

31:41.310 --> 31:43.060
I don't think we can take her!

31:43.270 --> 31:45.690
I haven't... lost... yet!

31:45.860 --> 31:48.650
There you go, being a sore loser!

31:57.540 --> 32:00.250
There were more pirates in hiding, huh?

32:05.460 --> 32:08.210
What the--?! Where the heck are we?!

32:12.430 --> 32:16.060
Oh, so you're a fan of Uta-sama, too, Trafalgar?

32:16.180 --> 32:18.140
Wrong. I'm a chaperone.

32:22.520 --> 32:23.520
For Bepo.

32:23.650 --> 32:24.610
Sorry.

32:24.810 --> 32:27.480
Thanks, Tra-guy!

32:27.690 --> 32:29.690
I wouldn't be laughing, Straw Hat-ya.

32:29.820 --> 32:32.110
If we can't figure out that woman's power--

32:33.990 --> 32:37.200
I'll take care of it!
I'm on a 184-win streak against Uta!

32:37.330 --> 32:38.700
Oh, there you are!

32:38.990 --> 32:39.950
--Found you!

32:38.990 --> 32:39.950
--Luffy-senpai!

32:38.990 --> 32:39.950
--It's Uta!

32:42.160 --> 32:43.250
We're getting out of here for now!

32:43.370 --> 32:44.880
The pirates are running away!

32:45.000 --> 32:47.710
Let's all team up and hunt them down!

33:12.950 --> 33:15.280
The SWORD Transponder Snail's not working.

33:15.410 --> 33:19.120
This is bad. Uta might be serious
about going through with her plan.

33:20.540 --> 33:23.330
So SWORD has their eye on Uta, too?

33:24.160 --> 33:26.750
You're Cipher Pol, right?
What are you doing here?

33:26.960 --> 33:30.460
Save the interjurisdictional quarrels for later!

33:30.670 --> 33:32.630
Can you use your Door-Door ability?

33:32.760 --> 33:34.300
You sure you don't know too much?

33:34.430 --> 33:35.840
No more than you.

33:36.930 --> 33:41.010
I can, but out here, it'd be too big
of a drain on my stamina.

33:41.140 --> 33:42.140
I see...

33:42.270 --> 33:44.640
What's the call? We're running out of time.

33:46.310 --> 33:49.650
We'll recruit more fighters.
For now, that's all we can do.

33:51.110 --> 33:54.240
This sucks! They all got caught!

33:54.820 --> 33:58.700
They're just stuck on those lines,
so it's probably fine, but...

33:58.870 --> 34:02.330
I can't believe I get to
give Luffy-senpai a lift!

34:02.450 --> 34:04.870
I'm so overwhelmed, I can't see in front of me!

34:05.460 --> 34:06.500
Straw Hat!

34:06.860 --> 34:07.500
Thanks.

34:11.170 --> 34:13.630
What are you doing? We need to move!

34:30.640 --> 34:32.400
There're so many of them!

34:32.520 --> 34:34.320
They're gonna surround us for sure!

34:34.440 --> 34:35.820
You boys...

34:45.000 --> 34:47.040
You really saved us!

34:47.500 --> 34:49.020
Your name is Luffy, then?

34:49.280 --> 34:49.920
Yep!

34:50.170 --> 34:51.710
--Who're you, old guy?

34:50.170 --> 34:51.710
--Then, you're...

34:53.050 --> 34:59.300
I am the former ruler of this nation,
Elegia. My name is Gordon.

34:59.510 --> 35:03.970
What nation? This place has got all kinds
of buildings, but there's not a soul around!

35:04.100 --> 35:04.580
No.

35:05.320 --> 35:08.640
Elegia used to be known as the capital
of music for the entire world.

35:09.390 --> 35:11.810
Before everyone who lived
there went missing overnight.

35:12.020 --> 35:14.480
You mean to say a whole country
was gone in one night?

35:14.610 --> 35:17.820
A certain big-name pirate
is rumored to be responsible.

35:25.080 --> 35:27.080
Let me tell you about Uta.

35:27.750 --> 35:32.460
Once Elegia's citizens were gone,
I raised Uta here, alone.

35:32.580 --> 35:33.840
You did?

35:34.170 --> 35:38.090
But it was only the two of us, by ourselves...

35:39.050 --> 35:40.880
I'm sure she was lonely.

35:41.010 --> 35:44.180
She put a brave face on around me,

35:44.300 --> 35:49.730
but whenever she was alone,
she would sing about her lost friends...

35:50.690 --> 35:59.080
<i>♪I recall that day
we played together by the sea</i>♪

35:59.390 --> 36:02.280
<i>♪Just you and me</i>♪

36:02.700 --> 36:11.320
<i>♪Still that scent of ocean seems
to fade each passing day</i>♪

36:11.360 --> 36:14.170
<i>♪It slips away</i>♪

36:14.330 --> 36:20.260
<i>♪So I sing an old familiar song
I hope you know the one</i>♪

36:20.380 --> 36:26.140
<i>♪I will sing to call you back to me</i>♪

36:26.760 --> 36:30.030
<i>--♪I need you to hear it
Need you to believe in</i>♪

36:26.760 --> 36:30.030
--I raised her to be the greatest
singer in the world

36:30.030 --> 36:32.620
--in an effort to put more joy into her voice.

36:32.620 --> 36:35.330
--<i>♪Something out there...♪</i>

36:37.520 --> 36:39.400
Excuse me?! Are you listening?!

36:39.530 --> 36:41.530
Just keep talking, old timer.

36:45.120 --> 36:46.280
Sorry.

36:46.410 --> 36:51.290
Anyway, I guess that explains how Uta-sama
doesn't know what Luffy-senpai's been up to.

36:51.410 --> 36:54.670
Sorry!

36:57.130 --> 36:59.590
The greatest question I faced
was when and how

36:59.710 --> 37:03.840
to present her sublime singing to the world.

37:04.050 --> 37:08.180
She grew up almost entirely
ignorant of outside affairs...

37:08.850 --> 37:13.600
But then, the time came in a way
I couldn't have anticipated.

37:17.560 --> 37:21.530
It was two years ago...
She stumbled upon something...

37:21.820 --> 37:25.160
A new type of Video Transponder Snail
had washed up on the beach.

37:26.740 --> 37:33.160
Uta started sending her songs beyond the island,
like she had been set free from something.

37:33.500 --> 37:35.670
Her voice charmed many fans,

37:36.290 --> 37:41.460
and spread quickly enough to fill
every corner of the globe.

37:42.340 --> 37:43.920
Thanks, Uta!

37:44.050 --> 37:45.180
I feel better now!

37:45.300 --> 37:49.640
I think I'll make it through another
day tomorrow thanks to you!

37:50.010 --> 37:53.680
Me, too. I'm so glad you all like my singing!

37:56.730 --> 38:01.020
But as she learned about
the state of the outside world,

38:01.150 --> 38:05.280
she started to develop
awareness to something else...

38:05.530 --> 38:08.740
Of how the Great Pirate Era was one
of unending war and bloodshed.

38:10.870 --> 38:14.250
It started with just her singing,

38:14.370 --> 38:19.420
but in time, fans were starting
to hail Uta as some kind of savior.

38:19.880 --> 38:21.550
And Uta, in response...

38:21.750 --> 38:24.460
I understand how all of you feel.

38:24.760 --> 38:27.880
And if that's what you need,
then I'll create a new age for you!

38:28.640 --> 38:31.720
Please! You have to stop Uta's plan!

38:31.850 --> 38:34.730
You were her friend, Luffy!
You should be able to do it!

38:34.890 --> 38:37.140
Does this plan of hers involve the concert--?

38:40.110 --> 38:40.940
Sorry!

38:41.190 --> 38:42.190
Bepo!

38:47.360 --> 38:49.030
--The bear!

38:47.360 --> 38:49.030
--Bepo?!

38:53.950 --> 38:54.700
Uta...

38:55.040 --> 38:58.170
Gordon. What are you doing with these pirates?

38:59.250 --> 39:02.130
Uta, how come you left Shanks' ship?

39:03.800 --> 39:06.760
You said you were the
Red-Haired Pirates' musician.

39:06.880 --> 39:09.180
You could always go back to him!

39:09.340 --> 39:10.640
Shut up...

39:10.890 --> 39:14.640
I don't want to talk about Shanks anymore!

39:25.440 --> 39:26.780
Seriously, Luffy,

39:26.900 --> 39:30.820
Give up the One Piece,
being a pirate king, and Shanks' hat...

39:30.950 --> 39:35.330
Forget all that dumb stuff
and just enjoy life with me!

39:35.450 --> 39:37.290
Hey! That's going too far!

39:37.410 --> 39:41.370
We could eat all kinds of tasty food,
and play chicken, or arm wrestle!

39:41.500 --> 39:43.460
Just laughing and living our lives,
like we used to.

39:43.670 --> 39:47.050
Give the hat back! That's Shanks' hat!

39:48.630 --> 39:54.010
Fine, Luffy. I don't need you in my new age.

39:54.720 --> 39:56.180
Room! Shambles!

39:59.480 --> 40:00.770
Huh? Where'd they go?

40:00.890 --> 40:02.600
Did the pirates get away?

40:02.730 --> 40:05.940
Huh... I guess there are
all kinds of different powers.

40:06.320 --> 40:11.320
Oh, well! Let's make it a game!
Try to find the runaway pirates!

40:18.660 --> 40:21.410
Let me out! I gotta get my hat back!

40:21.540 --> 40:25.170
Shut up! You're staying in there
<i>because</i> you can't pull that off!

40:25.420 --> 40:27.300
But we can't just keep running...

40:27.460 --> 40:29.380
We'll head to the opposite end
of the island, then to the port.

40:29.510 --> 40:30.220
The port?

40:30.470 --> 40:33.930
There were Marines and intelligence
agents in the audience.

40:34.050 --> 40:35.300
What're they doing here?

40:35.510 --> 40:39.640
It means the World Government and Navy
have already noticed Uta's power

40:39.770 --> 40:41.980
and consider her to be a threat.

40:42.230 --> 40:44.770
They were keeping an eye on her?

40:45.060 --> 40:48.900
If we can find someone near the island
from the Navy and get them to talk,

40:49.030 --> 40:50.440
we might learn how her power--

40:50.570 --> 40:51.740
Wrong way!

40:54.910 --> 40:57.780
Not a problem! My barriers are real strong!

40:57.910 --> 41:00.910
But it keeps rolling!

41:07.790 --> 41:10.210
We're real high!

41:21.930 --> 41:25.150
Luffy-senpai! I'm begging you,
you gotta hold it in!

41:34.280 --> 41:36.570
Hey, Gordon... are you mad?

41:36.700 --> 41:39.410
About me doing this concert without asking you?

41:39.530 --> 41:42.040
It's not just a concert, is it?

41:42.250 --> 41:45.580
You noticed? You'll support me, right?

41:46.880 --> 41:50.340
I... I've...

41:51.210 --> 41:54.380
Must be nice to be able to have
that choice. To chicken out.

41:54.510 --> 41:58.300
I don't want you doing this!

41:58.430 --> 41:59.850
But--

41:59.970 --> 42:01.390
Just wait there for now.

42:01.510 --> 42:04.480
The World Government
and Navy will come after you!

42:04.640 --> 42:07.190
It's fine. Because I have this.

42:08.690 --> 42:11.360
No... Tot Musica!

42:11.780 --> 42:15.990
I knew about how you hid it beneath the castle.

42:16.360 --> 42:18.110
Why didn't you throw it away?

42:18.280 --> 42:22.660
Maybe you were hoping for
the dawn of a new age, too.

42:23.580 --> 42:26.500
Uta! You can't use that! It's--

42:26.670 --> 42:29.040
Uta!

42:33.670 --> 42:37.050
The sea's real big. Real vast.

42:37.340 --> 42:40.220
But I don't see anybody, much less the Navy.

42:40.350 --> 42:41.310
She's gone!

42:41.400 --> 42:41.970
Who is?

42:42.140 --> 42:43.470
The Sunny's missing!

42:43.600 --> 42:45.230
Your ship?!

42:47.350 --> 42:48.730
Sunny!

42:50.520 --> 42:54.780
Sunny... Sunny... Sunny.

42:55.110 --> 42:56.240
Sunny!

42:56.360 --> 42:57.150
No way!

42:57.240 --> 42:59.500
Is that you, Sunny?!

42:59.700 --> 43:02.330
Did Uta-sama's power do this, too?!

43:02.450 --> 43:04.740
I'm seriously freaking out!

43:04.870 --> 43:06.500
Sunny?

43:08.000 --> 43:12.090
Reports are coming in from the forecastle decks:
No sign of the enemy in the vicinity.

43:12.420 --> 43:14.880
--Repeat, no sign of enemies in the vicinity.

43:12.420 --> 43:14.880
--Make sure we haven't been followed.

43:15.050 --> 43:22.140
Armed scouting team one has landed and is moving
through the ruins. No signs of the enemy.

43:22.260 --> 43:27.020
Armed scouting team two is continuing
the search, but no trace of the enemy so far.

43:27.230 --> 43:32.400
Mission is underway, but unable
to confirm enemy presence.

43:32.520 --> 43:34.110
Awaiting further orders.

43:39.490 --> 43:42.370
What in the world happened?

43:59.800 --> 44:03.930
This is armed scouting team seven.
No intel found on Elegian citizens.

44:04.050 --> 44:07.430
Armed scout team two, unable to
find any hostiles in the vicinity.

44:07.560 --> 44:09.980
This is armed scout team four with
a message for Vice Admiral Mononaga.

44:10.100 --> 44:12.400
The audience is still unconscious,
I repeat, still unconscious.

44:12.520 --> 44:14.150
They're not dead, are they?

44:14.270 --> 44:15.860
Just sleeping!

44:16.270 --> 44:18.190
But they're not waking up, no matter what.

44:20.200 --> 44:25.080
And if you kill me, nobody here
is going to get their soul back...

44:25.200 --> 44:26.790
You think that's a good idea?

44:26.910 --> 44:28.410
Miss.

44:28.540 --> 44:33.920
I believe I understand pretty well
how your Devil Fruit power works.

44:34.040 --> 44:37.840
Great, that saves me an explanation!
Go ahead and leave, then.

44:37.960 --> 44:43.130
Besides, it won't be long
until I'm gone, anyway.

44:44.470 --> 44:47.720
This scent... Is that a Wake-shroom?

44:48.180 --> 44:49.720
Wake-shroom?

44:49.850 --> 44:55.480
Those who eat them are unable to sleep,
and in time, they die.

44:56.530 --> 45:00.150
Woman! Do you want to take the entire
audience with you when you die?!

45:00.400 --> 45:04.700
What does death matter?
Isn't the soul more important than the body?

45:04.820 --> 45:08.740
In the new age, everyone is going
to be living together, in soul!

45:10.200 --> 45:13.000
I'd rather not shed any blood today.

45:13.120 --> 45:18.090
Is there any way you'll reconsider this plot
of yours to turn the world on its head?

45:18.290 --> 45:19.630
Huh? What even is that?

45:19.880 --> 45:23.340
I just want everyone to be happy!

45:23.470 --> 45:27.640
I can tell you're not one to listen to reason.

45:27.760 --> 45:29.930
And neither are you guys.

45:30.060 --> 45:31.060
Not so fast!

45:32.980 --> 45:35.600
With your singing voice blocked out,
your powers are nothing!

45:35.730 --> 45:37.690
Nice try. But you're too late.

45:40.780 --> 45:44.740
Captain Koby? What in the
world's gotten into you?

45:47.280 --> 45:50.160
Everyone! The bad guys are here!

45:50.290 --> 45:53.410
Let's beat them up together
for our new era!

45:55.080 --> 45:59.710
Don't hurt them! These are
innocent civilians she's controlling!

46:06.510 --> 46:09.850
<i>♪I'm sick and tired of being alone
Wanna be connected♪</i>

46:09.970 --> 46:12.430
<i>♪Have a bond to hold on to</i>♪

46:12.600 --> 46:16.480
<i>♪Just gonna lay it all out, how I feel
Honest (Shout out!)♪</i>

46:19.400 --> 46:21.570
<i>♪Listen baby makin' you happy
Whether you like it or not</i>♪

46:21.690 --> 46:24.280
<i>♪Gonna be up in your ears
No run-in away just wait for the beat to drop</i>♪

46:24.400 --> 46:27.410
<i>♪Listen for a surprise
Every word will entice</i>♪

46:27.410 --> 46:30.270
<i>♪Be my good, good, good, good, boys and girls</i>♪

46:30.370 --> 46:33.750
<i>♪You think you're so tough?
Well I've had enough of it</i>♪

46:33.870 --> 46:35.710
<i>♪I got something here that's better</i>♪

46:35.830 --> 46:39.290
<i>♪Come on up and we can sing together</i>♪

46:39.460 --> 46:43.000
<i>♪Fun unfettered
Get on stage, let's go</i>♪

46:43.590 --> 46:45.880
<i>♪(Ha-how) Wanna make your day
Do my thing loud and proud (Hey!)</i>♪

46:46.010 --> 46:48.550
<i>♪No shame in what I create
I got this down</i>♪

46:48.680 --> 46:53.810
<i>♪Everything exactly how we want it
This is a utopia</i>♪

46:54.100 --> 46:57.640
<i>♪Been a long time comin', now it's here to stay
You can't deny</i>♪

46:59.440 --> 47:02.520
<i>♪It's a miracle of mercy
You can't stop it if you try</i>♪

47:02.650 --> 47:05.940
<i>♪I know it's possible
I'm not tryin' ask too much</i>♪

47:06.070 --> 47:08.660
<i>♪Salvation's got to come
This generation's done</i>♪

47:08.780 --> 47:10.950
<i>♪It's tired of never being listened to</i>♪

47:11.530 --> 47:12.950
<i>♪The screams were never heard</i>♪

47:12.950 --> 47:15.830
<i>♪The suffering endured
But no more!</i>♪

47:16.000 --> 47:18.540
<i>♪Watch me rock this
They got nothin'</i>♪

47:18.670 --> 47:21.830
<i>♪Up to me,
You just need to stay out of my way</i>♪

47:21.960 --> 47:26.550
<i>♪There's no turnin' back now
Gonna be singin' jointly for all time</i>♪

47:26.710 --> 47:29.300
<i>♪Blowin' your mind with my pace
Drummin' to burst your ear drum</i>♪

47:29.430 --> 47:31.510
<i>♪Bring in the bass, guitar and keys
Macaferri got nothin' on me, no</i>♪

47:31.680 --> 47:37.100
<i>♪Ooo-wah! Oh let me hear you shout!
Ooo-wah Ow-oo-wow</i>♪

47:37.230 --> 47:39.770
<i>♪Banish every gaslight
Let clarity shine</i>♪

47:39.890 --> 47:43.270
<i>♪Gotta clean up this brainwash
Don't let 'em tell you lies</i>♪

47:43.400 --> 47:45.400
<i>♪Heads up, let my song clear your senses</i>♪

47:45.530 --> 47:48.900
<i>♪All you really need
Is my true voice</i>♪

47:53.200 --> 47:55.870
Dammit, it's no good! We're stuck.

47:56.160 --> 47:58.120
That was one pathetic display.

47:58.250 --> 48:00.830
You're just as stuck as I am, Moss Head!

48:01.080 --> 48:03.590
Franky, Jimbei, any luck?

48:04.540 --> 48:05.880
It won't budge at all!

48:06.000 --> 48:07.760
Likewise.

48:07.880 --> 48:09.050
Brook?

48:09.170 --> 48:10.970
I can almost...

48:11.880 --> 48:13.010
Are you almost free?

48:13.260 --> 48:15.930
I can almost see... Nami-san's panties.

48:16.060 --> 48:16.850
Say what?!

48:16.990 --> 48:18.280
You look, you die!

48:19.810 --> 48:20.770
Can I say something?

48:21.310 --> 48:24.560
Uta said she'd make us into a song, didn't she?

48:24.690 --> 48:27.690
Maybe we're arranged on a staff for a reason.

48:27.820 --> 48:31.570
It does appear to be some kind of melody...

48:31.700 --> 48:34.240
Maybe our heads are where the notes are?

48:34.370 --> 48:36.700
Can you sing it, Brook?

48:36.830 --> 48:38.370
I can't see the entire score...

48:39.120 --> 48:41.160
Right now I can most easily see...

48:41.290 --> 48:43.830
--Shut up! And don't look!

48:41.290 --> 48:43.830
--some underwear.

48:43.960 --> 48:47.590
You noticed you were arranged on a score...
The Straw Hat crew never fails to impress.

48:47.840 --> 48:48.670
Huh?

48:49.010 --> 48:51.170
What are you two doing with Blueno?

48:51.300 --> 48:52.720
Explanations can wait for now.

48:53.090 --> 48:55.090
Here, sing this.

48:55.850 --> 48:58.510
<i>Mi! Re!</i>

49:01.390 --> 49:02.480
Finally free!

49:03.690 --> 49:06.190
Come on, keep it going, Brook!

49:06.650 --> 49:10.030
It seems you've got a grasp of the girl's power.

49:10.150 --> 49:11.190
Hey!

49:11.780 --> 49:14.530
Could you at least set my sister free?

49:14.660 --> 49:16.280
Big Brother...

49:17.530 --> 49:20.750
You cooperate with the Navy.
Even if it's temporary.

49:23.210 --> 49:24.920
<i>♪Mi...♪</i>

49:25.040 --> 49:26.750
<i>♪Mi...</i>♪

49:26.880 --> 49:28.630
<i>♪Mi!</i>♪

49:28.750 --> 49:29.840
<i>♪Do re...</i>♪

49:29.960 --> 49:31.210
<i>♪Mi!</i>♪

49:32.630 --> 49:35.430
Thank you. You are a magnificent little bear.

49:35.930 --> 49:37.140
Aye-aye!

49:42.770 --> 49:45.560
Why... are we still in here?!

49:45.690 --> 49:51.110
I can't let you loose until we know
for sure what Uta-sama's power are!

49:51.440 --> 49:52.820
Sunny!

49:52.940 --> 49:54.110
Sun... Sunny?

49:55.920 --> 49:57.040
Who're you?!

49:57.700 --> 49:59.740
It's good to see you again, Luffy-san.

49:59.870 --> 50:04.330
Koby! Get me... out of here!

50:04.540 --> 50:06.370
How'd you find us?

50:06.500 --> 50:08.630
I was able to sense Luffy-san's presence.

50:08.750 --> 50:10.420
Observation Haki, huh?

50:10.550 --> 50:14.550
After that, Blueno-san let us
use his Door-Door ability.

50:14.760 --> 50:18.760
Let me out with your Door-Door...

50:19.970 --> 50:23.980
Care to explain why Cipher Pol
and the Navy are working together?

50:24.230 --> 50:27.980
It's Uta's powers you really
want to know about, right?

50:28.270 --> 50:30.570
You know how they work?!

50:32.070 --> 50:38.320
This will be hard to believe,
but this world... It isn't reality.

50:39.740 --> 50:41.870
Everything you're seeing...

50:41.990 --> 50:49.250
...it's an imaginary world created in our
minds by Uta's Sing-Sing Fruit ability.

50:49.750 --> 50:56.470
The power of the Sing-Sing Fruit is to draw people's
soul into this world after hearing the user sing.

50:57.010 --> 51:00.970
Those who are affected
feel like they're in a world

51:01.100 --> 51:04.810
where Uta makes the rules
instead of reality.

51:05.100 --> 51:09.690
It's like everyone is dreaming the same dream.

51:10.520 --> 51:15.030
Come to think of it, Uta mentioned
having a power like that.

51:17.510 --> 51:20.660
So that's why everybody would fall
asleep when listening to her sing!

51:20.870 --> 51:23.740
Would've been a big help
if you'd said something sooner!

51:24.930 --> 51:26.030
I forgot!

51:26.120 --> 51:29.080
So... what's going on in reality?

51:29.210 --> 51:37.130
Our bodies are still there,
but Uta has control over them.

51:37.260 --> 51:39.090
How do we get back to the real world?

51:39.220 --> 51:42.470
If Uta sleeps, her power will cease to function.

51:42.600 --> 51:50.100
But while we're in the world of the
Sing-Sing Fruit, we can't affect her in reality.

51:50.350 --> 51:53.560
If she's using a Devil Fruit power,
it has to have a limit.

51:53.860 --> 51:55.320
You're right.

51:55.530 --> 51:59.700
Maintaining the Sing-Sing world
is an incredible drain on her stamina.

51:59.820 --> 52:03.740
Sort of like how I can't constantly
use the Door-Door Fruit's power.

52:03.950 --> 52:06.870
So we'll be okay once Uta-sama
gets tired enough to fall asleep?

52:06.990 --> 52:08.250
That's not likely.

52:08.660 --> 52:12.750
Before the concert started, she was confirmed
to be eating Wake-shrooms.

52:13.000 --> 52:16.130
They keep people who eat them from sleeping.

52:16.670 --> 52:21.680
It won't be long before Uta, in the real world,
runs out of strength... and dies.

52:21.800 --> 52:23.930
She's gonna die?

52:24.550 --> 52:25.560
Uta?

52:25.680 --> 52:27.930
Will we be released, then?

52:28.140 --> 52:29.640
No, the opposite.

52:29.770 --> 52:36.230
When Uta dies, this world
will be cut off from reality.

52:36.360 --> 52:39.650
And everyone in it...
us included, will be stuck here.

52:40.320 --> 52:47.790
Trapping all her fans in the Sing-Sing World...
That's what Uta has been planning.

52:48.120 --> 52:50.450
That's totally nuts!

52:50.580 --> 52:53.460
Koby, how do we stop Uta?

52:53.750 --> 52:58.670
That's what I came here to
find out, but I'm still not sure.

52:59.010 --> 53:01.420
But the more fighting strength
we have, the better,

53:01.550 --> 53:04.840
so Helmeppo is gathering the pirates
who've been trapped here.

53:04.970 --> 53:08.600
The Straw Hat crew also appears
to be taking some action.

53:08.720 --> 53:10.180
Then they're okay!

53:10.390 --> 53:12.980
They were headed for the Elegia castle.

53:13.270 --> 53:18.900
Nico Robin seems to know something about
what happened on this island ages ago.

53:19.030 --> 53:22.280
If there're any records on what happened,

53:22.400 --> 53:25.620
it might help us learn how
to get around Uta's power.

53:26.530 --> 53:28.330
Not a lot to pin our hopes to...

53:28.450 --> 53:30.540
Have a little faith in Robin-chan,
you stupid Moss Head!

53:30.660 --> 53:32.710
It's just the facts, Twirly Brow!

53:32.830 --> 53:35.750
They said there's a room with
a bunch of books over there!

53:40.710 --> 53:46.510
Everyone, let's forget about those pirates
and wait for the dawn of the new era!

53:50.260 --> 53:52.600
How long until Uta dies in reality?

53:52.730 --> 53:54.640
Should be less than two hours left.

54:01.530 --> 54:06.110
With walls this soundproof, I doubt
Uta's powers can reach us here.

54:06.240 --> 54:10.910
The Navy boys mentioned that anywhere
beyond the sound of her voice would be safe.

54:11.040 --> 54:13.660
Are these all history books?

54:13.790 --> 54:16.540
How are we supposed to get through all of this?!

54:25.090 --> 54:27.930
Three-Sword Style! Ultra Tiger Hunt!

54:31.560 --> 54:35.770
Diable Jambe... Frites Assorties!

54:36.850 --> 54:40.400
Strong Right! Weapons Left!

54:43.820 --> 54:45.150
Robin, look through the books!

54:45.400 --> 54:46.820
--Robin!

54:45.400 --> 54:46.820
--But

54:47.030 --> 54:49.660
We'll keep them off you, don't worry!

55:00.630 --> 55:05.340
It won't be long before we're in
a new age... with no bad people.

55:06.170 --> 55:09.890
Do you read me?
Uta has an hour left, at most.

55:10.140 --> 55:14.270
But the Video Transponder Snails,
with their souls stolen, are out of control...

55:14.560 --> 55:17.310
They're continuing to broadcast footage
from the Sing-Sing World.

55:17.640 --> 55:20.060
They need to be muted to avoid trouble.

55:20.190 --> 55:24.070
The second someone hears her singing,
their soul will be captured.

55:25.070 --> 55:27.280
<i>♪Listen baby makin' you happy
Whether you like it or not</i>♪

55:27.400 --> 55:29.990
<i>♪Gonna be up in your ears
No run-in' away just wait for the beat to drop</i>♪

55:30.110 --> 55:33.030
<i>♪Listen for a surprise
Every word will entice</i>♪

55:36.080 --> 55:39.670
<i>♪You think you're so tough?
Well, I've had enough of it</i>♪

55:39.790 --> 55:41.380
<i>♪I got something here that's better</i>♪

55:41.500 --> 55:45.090
<i>♪Come on up and we can sing together</i>♪

55:45.210 --> 55:48.170
<i>♪Fun unfettered
Get on stage, let's go (Ha-how!)</i>♪

55:49.430 --> 55:52.850
It's been six hours since Uta began her concert.

55:52.970 --> 55:55.720
The number of victims has been
increasing at an exponential rate.

55:55.890 --> 55:58.600
If things proceed at this rate, in one hour,

55:58.930 --> 56:03.020
the estimate is that 70% of the world's
population will be pulled into the Sing-Sing World.

56:03.310 --> 56:05.320
Seventy percent?
That's worse than we anticipated.

56:05.440 --> 56:07.900
This could mean the end of the world.

56:08.110 --> 56:10.530
She needs to be stopped somehow.

56:12.660 --> 56:14.080
Nice!

56:15.830 --> 56:17.370
Very nice-eh!

56:17.500 --> 56:21.540
You're coming home with me
to sing me a lullaby-eh!

56:23.880 --> 56:25.040
A Celestial Dragon...

56:27.550 --> 56:30.090
Saint Charloss is requesting your presence.

56:30.220 --> 56:31.630
You should be grateful.

56:31.880 --> 56:34.640
I'll pay a billion for you-eh!

56:35.390 --> 56:38.350
Wait, are you one of those Celestial Dragons?

56:41.310 --> 56:43.230
I know about them! It was in a book.

56:43.350 --> 56:46.930
They rule the world and want
to make slaves out of everyone.

56:46.920 --> 56:48.930
They're the most hated people in the world!

56:50.400 --> 56:53.410
You need to cut it out before you upset him.

56:53.530 --> 56:55.320
You guys are Marines?

56:55.450 --> 56:58.540
You must've taken leave to
come and see me! Thanks!

56:58.660 --> 57:02.410
Never mind that. You will obey Saint Charloss
and accompany us to the Holy Land.

57:02.540 --> 57:03.140
No way.

57:04.000 --> 57:05.670
Everyone's equal here!

57:05.960 --> 57:09.300
And we're glad to have this
old Celestial Dragon join us!

57:09.420 --> 57:12.800
Old?! She gets an execution-eh!

57:15.340 --> 57:18.100
Seriously, there's no point.

57:22.810 --> 57:26.060
If you're useless, I don't need you-eh.

57:27.040 --> 57:28.570
How could you do that?!

57:28.900 --> 57:31.400
It's okay. I'll save you.

57:33.820 --> 57:36.240
What are you Marines doing-eh?!

57:36.370 --> 57:38.910
Kill this little wench-eh!

57:41.080 --> 57:45.250
I thought the Navy was supposed
to represent justice...

57:47.960 --> 57:51.300
The Celestial Dragons might as well be gods...

57:51.710 --> 57:55.630
I get it! You don't really want to follow
this jerk's orders, do you?

57:55.970 --> 57:57.300
In that case, don't worry about it!

57:57.430 --> 58:01.930
In the new era, Celestial Dragons
and slaves will all be equal!

58:02.100 --> 58:04.600
Equality?! How revolting!

58:04.730 --> 58:07.810
All of you, hurry and kill her-eh!

58:08.020 --> 58:09.570
It's not personal, girl...

58:15.530 --> 58:17.320
Huh?

58:19.280 --> 58:22.330
Don't... think... you'll get...
away with tharrgble!

58:31.050 --> 58:35.050
You guys don't have to be afraid
of the Celestial Dragons anymore!

58:38.510 --> 58:41.180
This... This isn't a good idea, Uta!

58:41.430 --> 58:43.020
If you mess with a Celestial Dragon...

58:43.140 --> 58:45.810
...the World Government and Navy
will hunt you down!

58:45.940 --> 58:47.060
I'm telling you, it's fine!

58:47.190 --> 58:48.940
Sorry, Uta!

58:49.440 --> 58:54.990
I should be heading home by now.
I've got sheep to look after.

58:55.150 --> 58:57.240
Thanks! I had a great time!

58:57.360 --> 58:59.870
Hang on... I don't understand...

59:01.030 --> 59:04.040
Why would you want to go back
to a life that's so hard and painful

59:04.160 --> 59:06.580
when you could enjoy life here instead?

59:06.710 --> 59:10.500
Most importantly, anyone know what happened
to the pirates I had captured before?

59:13.420 --> 59:16.590
Uta-san, this needs to stop now!

59:17.010 --> 59:20.140
You're a Marine, too?
You here to save the Celestial Dragon?

59:20.340 --> 59:23.010
I'm here to save lives!

59:23.470 --> 59:28.060
You need to release everyone's souls
so they can return to reality.

59:28.190 --> 59:29.350
Captain Koby?!

59:34.400 --> 59:36.440
Is he famous or something?

59:36.570 --> 59:40.780
He's the hero who saved people
during the Rocky Port incident!

59:41.780 --> 59:47.620
Really? I've been on Elegia all this time,
so I haven't kept up with the news.

59:47.960 --> 59:49.250
W-Well...

59:49.370 --> 59:51.000
Hey, hero.

59:51.500 --> 59:55.090
I've used my power too much.
You have to tell them.

59:55.380 --> 59:56.300
Right.

59:56.920 --> 59:59.170
Everyone, please listen!

59:59.300 --> 1:00:03.350
The truth is, this world that
we're in is not reality.

1:00:10.020 --> 1:00:12.730
You've all been lied to!

1:00:12.940 --> 1:00:16.030
We should leave this place as soon as possible!

1:00:17.400 --> 1:00:20.650
Uta... did you really...
lie to us and trap us here?!

1:00:20.860 --> 1:00:24.330
It's not a lie!
I haven't lied to anybody!

1:00:24.450 --> 1:00:29.160
You've got it all wrong, guys!
I'm just trying to lead you to happiness!

1:00:33.080 --> 1:00:35.590
This is the place you've all dreamed of.

1:00:35.710 --> 1:00:37.920
The Great Pirate Era is over!

1:00:38.050 --> 1:00:40.590
It's going to be an age of freedom
and peace instead!

1:00:42.510 --> 1:00:43.930
Isn't that fantastic?!

1:00:44.050 --> 1:00:46.100
There'll be plenty of food and games!

1:00:46.220 --> 1:00:50.560
There'll be no mean people,
no sickness, no pain!

1:00:50.680 --> 1:00:53.560
Yeah... I guess it would be happier living here.

1:00:53.690 --> 1:00:54.520
Me, too!

1:00:54.730 --> 1:00:56.190
Right?! I knew it!

1:00:56.360 --> 1:00:58.150
But... I've got work...

1:00:58.280 --> 1:01:02.570
I'm trying to tell you, you don't
have to work! Or study...

1:01:02.700 --> 1:01:04.990
But still... I don't want to stay here forever.

1:01:05.200 --> 1:01:06.910
There're things I've put a lot of work into.

1:01:07.030 --> 1:01:08.870
And the idea of playing around all the time...

1:01:08.990 --> 1:01:10.370
I wanna go home.

1:01:10.500 --> 1:01:12.290
This would completely
change civilization, right?

1:01:12.410 --> 1:01:13.790
I don't think I can go along with this...

1:01:13.920 --> 1:01:16.000
Even if it is Uta's idea...

1:01:16.290 --> 1:01:18.840
Uta-san, you should cancel your--

1:01:18.960 --> 1:01:20.130
Hang on a second!

1:01:20.260 --> 1:01:23.630
Everyone! I thought you wanted to be free!

1:01:23.970 --> 1:01:27.470
Were you lying when you said you wanted
no more diseases or bullying?!

1:01:27.720 --> 1:01:31.270
You told me you didn't want to spend
every day afraid of pirates!

1:01:31.390 --> 1:01:33.100
I'm telling you, I want to go home, dammit!

1:01:35.230 --> 1:01:38.360
Stop that! Uta has done
all of this for our sake!

1:01:38.480 --> 1:01:40.860
--Same here!

1:01:38.480 --> 1:01:40.860
--I never asked her to!

1:01:40.980 --> 1:01:43.450
--I agree with Uta!

1:01:40.980 --> 1:01:43.450
--You guys need to shut up!

1:01:43.570 --> 1:01:45.530
--I liked going to school!

1:01:43.570 --> 1:01:45.530
--I don't like this.

1:01:45.660 --> 1:01:48.450
--A big difference!

1:01:45.660 --> 1:01:48.450
--What difference does that make?

1:01:48.580 --> 1:01:50.240
Uta's going too far!

1:01:50.370 --> 1:01:53.120
--What did you say about me?!

1:01:50.370 --> 1:01:53.120
--You're awful!

1:01:53.250 --> 1:01:56.250
Okay! Sorry, I get it now!

1:01:57.710 --> 1:02:00.420
You just need to have more fun, right?!

1:02:08.260 --> 1:02:11.930
See? You're all having fun now, right?!

1:02:20.520 --> 1:02:26.820
Everyone! Let's all enjoy a free and
peaceful new age together, forever!

1:02:30.120 --> 1:02:31.240
Saint Charloss!

1:02:31.370 --> 1:02:34.910
We can't afford more casualties.
The time has come to make a decision.

1:02:35.210 --> 1:02:38.880
Even if a Celestial Dragon
is caught in the crossfire...

1:02:47.970 --> 1:02:49.850
Well, we barely made it out of there.

1:02:49.970 --> 1:02:51.850
Who the heck are you?!

1:02:51.970 --> 1:02:53.140
Blueno.

1:02:53.270 --> 1:02:55.060
Koby, did you see Uta?

1:02:55.180 --> 1:02:56.140
Well...

1:02:56.270 --> 1:02:58.400
I'm guessing negotiations have fallen through.

1:02:58.520 --> 1:02:59.420
How about you guys?

1:02:59.420 --> 1:03:00.400
Check it out!

1:03:02.020 --> 1:03:05.240
Hold on! I didn't hear anything
about working with Straw Hat!

1:03:05.360 --> 1:03:06.650
I'd rather die!

1:03:06.780 --> 1:03:07.650
See ya!

1:03:08.660 --> 1:03:09.490
Wait a minute--

1:03:09.740 --> 1:03:12.530
We'll figure out our own way of beating Uta!

1:03:12.830 --> 1:03:14.080
Sunny...

1:03:14.410 --> 1:03:15.580
What about my crew?

1:03:15.700 --> 1:03:17.370
Still not back.

1:03:17.500 --> 1:03:21.000
If they can't find Uta's weakness,
we're out of options.

1:03:22.130 --> 1:03:24.760
And I can't use my Door-Door
ability in this body...

1:03:25.010 --> 1:03:27.510
It'll be fine. Knowing my gang...

1:03:27.930 --> 1:03:30.390
Rolling... Exploding Star!

1:03:32.010 --> 1:03:33.180
How's that?!

1:03:33.390 --> 1:03:38.480
"The fears and doubts of men...
given the name Tot Musica.

1:03:38.770 --> 1:03:40.940
Now flee and cower."

1:03:41.150 --> 1:03:43.070
Kung Fu Point!

1:03:43.360 --> 1:03:45.190
Mirage Tempo!

1:03:50.990 --> 1:03:52.490
Diable Jambe!

1:03:53.030 --> 1:03:55.160
Collier Strike!

1:03:55.290 --> 1:03:57.080
One-Sword Style... Demon Horse!

1:04:01.040 --> 1:04:05.210
Soul Parade... Ice Burn!

1:04:07.420 --> 1:04:10.220
Fishman Karate! Sharkskin Palm Thrust!

1:04:11.090 --> 1:04:14.350
Radical Beam! Giant Slalom!

1:04:16.720 --> 1:04:18.520
Uh-oh! It's gonna collapse!

1:04:18.640 --> 1:04:21.190
What idiot started blowing stuff up indoors?!

1:04:21.770 --> 1:04:23.810
Super sorry about that!

1:04:27.530 --> 1:04:31.030
We'll be buried alive!
Come to think of it, I'd look right at home!

1:04:31.150 --> 1:04:33.280
This way, Robin!

1:04:36.330 --> 1:04:40.500
Brulee! I know you're in there!
Let us into Mirro-world right now!

1:04:43.110 --> 1:04:44.460
Quit ignoring me!

1:04:44.590 --> 1:04:48.630
You realize without our intel, you'll be stuck
in the Sing-Sing World, too, right?!

1:04:48.760 --> 1:04:51.010
You'll never see your precious
friends and family again.

1:04:51.130 --> 1:04:52.130
You okay with that?!

1:04:53.720 --> 1:04:55.760
Not even Big Bro Katakuri...?

1:04:55.890 --> 1:04:57.010
N-No!

1:05:11.860 --> 1:05:13.660
You guys! You made it!

1:05:13.780 --> 1:05:14.620
Luffy!

1:05:14.740 --> 1:05:15.570
Sunny!

1:05:17.330 --> 1:05:18.450
Who's that supposed to be?

1:05:18.660 --> 1:05:19.830
It's Sunny!

1:05:19.950 --> 1:05:21.910
She's so cute!

1:05:22.040 --> 1:05:23.920
What kind of mods did that?!

1:05:24.040 --> 1:05:27.210
Can't believe we ended up back here...

1:05:27.340 --> 1:05:29.380
Sorry, Big Bro Oven.

1:05:29.630 --> 1:05:33.220
Robin-san, did you discover how to beat Uta?

1:05:33.430 --> 1:05:37.430
The old records say that those
trapped in the Sing-Sing World

1:05:37.550 --> 1:05:41.310
won't be able to return to reality
under their own power. No matter what.

1:05:43.100 --> 1:05:48.570
But if someone with the Sing-Sing Fruit powers
uses Tot Musica, there'll be a chance.

1:05:48.690 --> 1:05:50.530
Tot Musica?

1:05:50.860 --> 1:05:54.240
An entity from ancient times
created from human emotions.

1:05:54.700 --> 1:05:57.870
Loneliness, sadness...
the shadows that fall on the soul.

1:05:57.990 --> 1:05:59.490
It's been called a Demon King before as well.

1:05:59.620 --> 1:06:01.910
Is it some kind of weapon?

1:06:02.040 --> 1:06:04.960
The part I was able to read
only mentioned avoiding it.

1:06:06.460 --> 1:06:10.960
So if the Sing-Sing Fruit user breaks this
taboo, what kind of chance will we get?

1:06:11.170 --> 1:06:15.340
The records say that when the Demon King
is summoned with Tot Musica,

1:06:15.470 --> 1:06:21.850
it'll appear both in the world created by
the Sing-Sing Fruit as well as in reality.

1:06:21.970 --> 1:06:27.600
The Demon King acts as a link between
the two worlds at that point.

1:06:27.730 --> 1:06:32.190
And if the Demon King is attacked
in both worlds at the same time...

1:06:32.320 --> 1:06:35.990
...he'll be defeated, and that
will erase the song world.

1:06:36.200 --> 1:06:37.240
Really?!

1:06:37.360 --> 1:06:40.950
I doubt there'd be a record
unless it worked before.

1:06:41.080 --> 1:06:43.120
We've gotta try it!

1:06:47.640 --> 1:06:51.290
Who's gonna attack Uta-sama in reality, though?

1:06:51.500 --> 1:06:55.220
Well, we're all stuck in here...

1:06:55.340 --> 1:06:58.260
The only people who could strike in
reality would be the Navy or Cipher--

1:06:58.390 --> 1:06:59.470
No.

1:06:59.760 --> 1:07:02.390
They won't make a move
with civilian lives at stake.

1:07:02.510 --> 1:07:06.020
As valuable as this intel is,
without someone to work within reality...

1:07:06.140 --> 1:07:07.770
There is someone.

1:07:09.690 --> 1:07:10.980
Captain!

1:07:13.150 --> 1:07:14.610
Is that Bepo? Seriously?

1:07:14.740 --> 1:07:16.700
And who's the old guy?

1:07:16.820 --> 1:07:19.360
That's Uta-sama's adoptive father, Gordon-san!

1:07:19.610 --> 1:07:21.240
Uta-chan's dad?

1:07:21.370 --> 1:07:23.950
So who exactly are you talking about?

1:07:24.080 --> 1:07:25.190
Shanks...

1:07:25.950 --> 1:07:27.210
Shanks?!

1:07:27.330 --> 1:07:32.040
When Shanks arrives,
he'll be able to stop Uta in reality.

1:07:32.340 --> 1:07:35.420
Old guy, did something happen
between Uta and Shanks?

1:07:35.760 --> 1:07:37.170
Well...

1:07:39.380 --> 1:07:40.550
Old guy!

1:07:43.890 --> 1:07:49.020
Ah! He's going straight to Uta-sama!
And we can't beat her yet!

1:07:49.140 --> 1:07:51.650
There's no stopping our captain
when he gets like that.

1:07:51.770 --> 1:07:55.360
We're running out of time anyway.
Might as well join him and put an end to this.

1:07:55.690 --> 1:07:56.990
But how?

1:07:57.110 --> 1:08:01.320
If we need simultaneous attacks,
we'll start hitting her and won't stop...

1:08:01.780 --> 1:08:06.200
...until the attack on the other side starts
and the timing matches up.

1:08:06.330 --> 1:08:09.000
I feel like a punk for chickening out!

1:08:09.120 --> 1:08:12.710
There's no way we can lose
with the Straw Hats backing us!

1:08:13.080 --> 1:08:14.880
We've got no other choice.

1:08:15.000 --> 1:08:15.920
Yeah!

1:08:16.460 --> 1:08:19.300
So... I was wondering...
What happened to you?

1:08:19.420 --> 1:08:20.590
Now you ask?

1:08:37.230 --> 1:08:41.700
What are you doing here?
You can fight me over and over, but you'll never win.

1:08:41.990 --> 1:08:43.820
It's not over yet.

1:08:43.950 --> 1:08:46.200
There you go again, you sore loser!

1:08:50.040 --> 1:08:54.290
Then, I guess we'll settle this with
a fight, like we used to, Luffy.

1:09:17.190 --> 1:09:18.610
You're not even trying to hit me.

1:09:24.240 --> 1:09:25.700
What you're doing is wrong!

1:09:25.820 --> 1:09:27.580
I could say that to you, Luffy.

1:09:28.540 --> 1:09:32.790
You need to realize that
the Great Pirate Era is over.

1:09:33.830 --> 1:09:37.000
Why do you wanna be the King
of the Pirates so bad, anyway?

1:09:37.210 --> 1:09:38.880
To make a new era.

1:09:39.630 --> 1:09:41.630
Luffy--!

1:09:47.680 --> 1:09:50.560
The Great Pirate Era began
with Roger's execution...

1:09:52.140 --> 1:09:56.100
Now, Luffy, it's gonna end with yours!

1:09:56.230 --> 1:09:57.310
Don't do it!

1:09:59.270 --> 1:10:01.360
Uta!

1:10:02.190 --> 1:10:11.450
You... You used to love the
Red-Haired Pirates so much!

1:10:12.450 --> 1:10:15.170
Why do you hate pirates now?!

1:10:17.580 --> 1:10:19.170
It's Shanks' fault.

1:10:20.500 --> 1:10:23.130
I thought of him...

1:10:25.380 --> 1:10:27.510
...like my own father!

1:10:35.020 --> 1:10:40.020
I considered everyone on that ship to be family!

1:10:40.190 --> 1:10:43.900
But that was just a lie they told me!

1:10:44.240 --> 1:10:47.490
That's why... Shanks abandonded me!

1:10:47.990 --> 1:10:51.450
He left me behind on Elegia!

1:10:51.580 --> 1:10:54.660
He said it was so you could be a singer!

1:10:54.790 --> 1:10:55.710
Wrong!

1:11:03.840 --> 1:11:09.050
Magnificent! Your voice is a gift to the world!

1:11:09.220 --> 1:11:13.470
There's no shortage of experts,
instruments, and music here.

1:11:13.970 --> 1:11:16.810
We would love for you to join us in Elegia!

1:11:16.940 --> 1:11:19.060
The entire country would welcome you!

1:11:20.900 --> 1:11:24.480
You seemed to really enjoy singing back there.

1:11:24.610 --> 1:11:26.150
Hm? I guess...

1:11:26.280 --> 1:11:31.910
You sure you wouldn't rather sing
for a big crowd instead of for us?

1:11:32.030 --> 1:11:33.660
It's not like that.

1:11:34.370 --> 1:11:35.540
Y'know, Uta...

1:11:35.660 --> 1:11:39.290
Things like peace and equality
don't really exist in the world.

1:11:40.420 --> 1:11:42.590
But your voice...

1:11:42.710 --> 1:11:46.260
It's the one thing that can bring happiness
to everyone in the world.

1:11:46.380 --> 1:11:47.420
What are you talking about?

1:11:47.670 --> 1:11:50.010
You can stay, if you want.

1:11:50.430 --> 1:11:52.930
I'll come pick you up once you're
the greatest singer in the world.

1:11:53.140 --> 1:11:56.520
Stupid! I'm the Red-Haired Pirates' musician!

1:11:56.640 --> 1:12:00.810
If you're asking me to choose between learning
about music and leaving... leaving you guys...

1:12:00.940 --> 1:12:02.500
Okay, I get it!

1:12:02.810 --> 1:12:05.900
You've got a point. We can ship out tomorrow.

1:12:08.030 --> 1:12:10.160
But that night...

1:12:17.370 --> 1:12:18.620
Gordon-san?

1:12:20.170 --> 1:12:21.710
You're awake?

1:12:25.340 --> 1:12:26.920
What happened?

1:12:27.050 --> 1:12:28.630
Where are Shanks and the others?!

1:12:28.760 --> 1:12:30.760
They took everything!

1:12:32.390 --> 1:12:35.560
Everyone... they're all dead...

1:12:35.680 --> 1:12:36.850
Where is Shanks?!

1:12:37.060 --> 1:12:44.020
They used your singing voice to approach Elegia,
plotting to make off with our treasures...

1:12:44.150 --> 1:12:45.360
You mean...?

1:12:45.480 --> 1:12:47.610
The Red-Haired Pirates...

1:12:51.150 --> 1:12:56.990
They've been lying to you this whole time!
The Red-Haired Pirates! And Shanks!

1:13:04.540 --> 1:13:07.880
Shanks! Don't leave me!

1:13:20.390 --> 1:13:23.850
Why...? Why would you do this?!

1:13:30.800 --> 1:13:33.800
"The country of music, Elegia, destroyed"

1:13:33.800 --> 1:13:37.300
"Love and peace are trampled
with only two survivors!"

1:13:37.300 --> 1:13:41.020
"The Culprit is Red-Haired Shanks"

1:13:43.500 --> 1:13:47.290
Shanks would never do something like that!
And you know that!

1:13:47.500 --> 1:13:49.880
Then explain the last 12 years!

1:13:50.000 --> 1:13:54.340
You're nothing but a tool
for Shanks, too, Luffy!

1:13:54.470 --> 1:13:55.550
Shanks is coming.

1:13:55.800 --> 1:13:57.300
To save you?

1:13:57.430 --> 1:13:59.100
To save you.

1:13:59.220 --> 1:14:00.680
Me? Why?

1:14:00.890 --> 1:14:05.690
You think he's gonna sit back while his
daughter pulls something like this?!

1:14:11.030 --> 1:14:14.950
He abandoned me...
he's not coming.

1:14:23.000 --> 1:14:25.330
Enough is enough, Luffy.

1:14:27.290 --> 1:14:28.290
Bye-bye.

1:14:39.140 --> 1:14:40.510
Shanks...?

1:14:42.560 --> 1:14:43.640
Why?

1:14:45.350 --> 1:14:47.730
It's been a while...

1:14:48.440 --> 1:14:49.980
And I felt like hearing you sing.

1:15:07.330 --> 1:15:09.080
This is perfect!

1:15:09.210 --> 1:15:13.130
Soon, all my fans and I are
going to bring a new age.

1:15:13.250 --> 1:15:17.380
And I wanted to settle up
with you before I did!

1:15:19.590 --> 1:15:23.430
Everyone! The worst pirate of all is here!

1:15:23.810 --> 1:15:25.230
Let's beat him together!

1:15:29.400 --> 1:15:30.860
Shanks is here, isn't he?

1:15:32.270 --> 1:15:33.270
Now!

1:15:49.590 --> 1:15:51.750
You still want to fight? In that case...

1:15:53.290 --> 1:15:55.340
--♪We can choose the way of our future♪

1:15:55.340 --> 1:15:56.460
--Hold it right there!<i></i>

1:15:57.510 --> 1:15:58.010
--Sunny! Sunny--!

1:15:57.510 --> 1:15:58.010
--<i>♪Try a brand new path</i>♪

1:15:58.010 --> 1:15:59.840
--Sunny! Sunny--!

1:16:02.800 --> 1:16:04.640
Guard Point!

1:16:04.760 --> 1:16:06.640
Room! Shambles!

1:16:07.680 --> 1:16:10.230
Barrier Ball! Sound!

1:16:13.060 --> 1:16:17.150
Uta-sama, that voice of yours
is trapped in here now!

1:16:20.780 --> 1:16:21.780
Whoa, there.

1:16:34.290 --> 1:16:36.880
Stow it, Gab!
You die before you fight back!

1:16:43.530 --> 1:16:44.730
No! No!

1:16:48.180 --> 1:16:50.850
Just hang on! The new age is almost here!

1:16:58.610 --> 1:17:03.700
That's right. Deploy every last asset
the Navy has to eliminate Uta.

1:17:04.120 --> 1:17:06.330
Doesn't matter if the audience go with her!

1:17:06.450 --> 1:17:10.500
We're doing this to protect the world
before she threatens anyone else!

1:17:10.790 --> 1:17:12.000
Annihilate her!

1:17:12.500 --> 1:17:16.040
So, the self-righteous Navy is willing
to kill a bunch of civilians?

1:17:16.340 --> 1:17:17.420
Is that it, Kizaru?!

1:17:17.670 --> 1:17:21.760
No such thing as justice without sacrifices.

1:17:21.880 --> 1:17:28.350
Ain't it a shame, having to sacrifice
thousands to kill one kid?

1:17:29.560 --> 1:17:32.060
Yasakani Sacred Jewel!

1:17:43.740 --> 1:17:47.120
Sorry, but this is kind of a family quarrel.

1:17:49.200 --> 1:17:51.410
Mind keeping out of it?

1:17:55.540 --> 1:18:00.710
I'm afraid that's not an option.
Not with the world on the line.

1:18:02.720 --> 1:18:05.010
I'm asking you to back off anyway.

1:18:07.720 --> 1:18:12.270
If I could do that sort of thing...
I'd still have my sight.

1:18:16.060 --> 1:18:17.610
Hongo-san...

1:18:18.690 --> 1:18:22.280
It looks like something's happening in reality.

1:18:27.620 --> 1:18:29.780
She's definitely been eating Wake-shrooms.

1:18:30.870 --> 1:18:33.370
They don't just keep people from sleeping,

1:18:33.580 --> 1:18:37.000
they make you turn aggressive
and lose control of your emotions.

1:18:47.550 --> 1:18:52.600
Bad guys need to look like bad guys.
I should've done this sooner.

1:18:53.600 --> 1:18:55.850
Uta!

1:19:00.570 --> 1:19:03.780
I wasn't brave enough...

1:19:03.900 --> 1:19:06.030
I didn't have the courage to use it!

1:19:06.450 --> 1:19:09.160
But I'm done being afraid!

1:19:11.370 --> 1:19:13.080
Be careful. I'm pretty sure that's--

1:19:15.830 --> 1:19:18.370
--My perfect barrier...!

1:19:23.170 --> 1:19:24.760
--That's...

1:19:24.880 --> 1:19:26.590
--Well, this is bad.

1:19:26.880 --> 1:19:28.930
--We went to the trouble of preparing these,

1:19:34.640 --> 1:19:35.430
<i>♪Rain begins to fall down♪</i>

1:19:35.560 --> 1:19:37.770
--<i>♪My bitter tears flowing out
They never dry up♪</i>

1:19:37.770 --> 1:19:39.190
--<i>♪I let the words of a curse
Be my deliverance♪</i>

1:19:37.770 --> 1:19:39.190
--This can't get much worse!
She's awoken it!

1:19:39.310 --> 1:19:40.650
--<i>♪I let the words of a curse
Be my deliverance♪</i>

1:19:39.310 --> 1:19:40.650
--The ancient Demon King, given form

1:19:40.650 --> 1:19:42.860
--by the song of a Sing-Sing Fruit user...

1:19:47.450 --> 1:19:49.240
--...Tot Musica!

1:19:50.240 --> 1:19:53.910
<i>♪These ancient words
like a hymn of reclamation♪</i>

1:19:54.040 --> 1:19:56.950
<i>♪Not even death will escape them♪</i>

1:19:57.080 --> 1:20:03.210
<i>♪How to center these
troubled thoughts? I pray♪</i>

1:20:04.460 --> 1:20:10.970
<i>♪Can the future bring calm
to the sea? I beg♪</i>

1:20:11.090 --> 1:20:14.720
<i>♪Keep making this music
'til you breathe your last♪</i>

1:20:14.850 --> 1:20:18.270
<i>♪We dream but never lose sight of the past♪</i>

1:20:18.390 --> 1:20:21.850
<i>♪Illuminate hope and forget all the rest♪</i>

1:20:21.980 --> 1:20:25.780
<i>♪Nothing left but to yell, yeah, yeah♪</i>

1:20:25.900 --> 1:20:29.450
<i>♪It's time for salvation to finally come♪</i>

1:20:29.570 --> 1:20:33.160
<i>♪I feel this rage, and I'm feelin' it strong♪</i>

1:20:33.280 --> 1:20:36.620
<i>♪This weeping and wailing
has gone far too long♪</i>

1:20:36.740 --> 1:20:40.960
<i>♪Nothing left but to yell! Yeah! Yeah!♪</i>

1:20:41.080 --> 1:20:44.670
<i>♪I know you feel it, too
So keep on singin' this song♪</i>

1:20:44.790 --> 1:20:48.380
<i>♪Even when they abuse us
We'll keep singing along♪</i>

1:20:48.510 --> 1:20:52.010
<i>♪We'll start another Big Bang
When we all sing as one♪</i>

1:20:52.130 --> 1:20:53.340
<i>♪United, we're fightin'♪--</i>

1:20:53.550 --> 1:20:54.930
--There's no cutting the sound.

1:20:54.940 --> 1:20:58.390
--It doesn't matter! There's no point.

1:20:58.380 --> 1:21:01.700
--Reality and the song world have been linked.

1:21:01.700 --> 1:21:02.830
--<i>♪Wandering heart
Clouds above♪</i>

1:21:01.700 --> 1:21:02.830
--by the Demon King...

1:21:02.830 --> 1:21:08.600
<i>♪Rain begins to fall down♪</i>

1:21:08.590 --> 1:21:09.170
--<i>♪My bitter tears flowing out
They never dry up♪</i>

1:21:09.170 --> 1:21:11.540
--Uta! Uta, please, stop!

1:21:11.540 --> 1:21:12.310
--<i>♪My bitter tears flowing out
They never dry up♪</i>

1:21:11.540 --> 1:21:12.310
--Uta, can you hear us?!

1:21:12.310 --> 1:21:13.280
--<i>♪I let the words of a curse
Be my deliverance♪</i>

1:21:13.280 --> 1:21:15.580
--This world... it's not what you talked about!

1:21:15.700 --> 1:21:18.070
--Uta!

1:21:23.290 --> 1:21:26.960
<i>♪These ancient words
like a hymn of reclamation♪</i>

1:21:27.090 --> 1:21:29.880
<i>♪Not even death will escape them♪</i>

1:21:30.010 --> 1:21:30.760
--<i>♪How to center these
troubled thoughts? I pray♪</i>

1:21:34.550 --> 1:21:36.350
--Uta!

1:21:37.350 --> 1:21:43.950
<i>♪Can the future bring calm
to the sea? I beg♪</i>

1:21:44.020 --> 1:21:44.850
<i>♪Keep making this music
'til you breathe your last♪</i>

1:21:47.940 --> 1:21:49.650
<i>♪We dream but never lose sight of the past♪</i>

1:21:49.650 --> 1:21:50.990
<i>♪Illuminate hope and forget all the rest♪</i>

1:21:56.370 --> 1:21:58.660
<i>♪Nothing left but to yell, yeah, yeah♪</i>

1:21:58.780 --> 1:22:00.290
<i>♪It's time for salvation to finally come♪</i>

1:22:04.370 --> 1:22:06.080
<i>♪I feel this rage, and I'm feelin' it strong♪</i>

1:22:06.210 --> 1:22:07.790
<i>♪This weeping and wailing
has gone far too long</i>♪

1:22:12.820 --> 1:22:14.090
<i>--♪Nothing left but yell! Yeah! Yeah!</i>♪

1:22:12.820 --> 1:22:14.090
--Heat Beating!

1:22:14.090 --> 1:22:15.760
<i>--♪I know you feel it, too
So keep on singin' this song </i>♪

1:22:15.760 --> 1:22:17.800
♪I know you feel it, too
So keep on singin' this song <i>♪</i>

1:22:17.930 --> 1:22:21.310
♪<i>Even when they abuse us
We'll keep singing along</i>♪

1:22:21.430 --> 1:22:23.890
♪<i>We'll start another Big Bang
When we all sing as one</i>♪

1:22:27.810 --> 1:22:30.400
<i>♪United, we're fightin',
bring 'em down with our song of ruin</i>♪

1:22:34.700 --> 1:22:38.490
--Dammit! This won't work
if we can't hit her simultaneously!

1:22:38.780 --> 1:22:40.530
--Princess Uta!

1:22:40.660 --> 1:22:43.450
--How could you use a voice that
was supposed to save people for <i>this?!</i>

1:22:46.850 --> 1:22:47.620
--Usopp!

1:22:48.540 --> 1:22:50.280
--I'm fine...

1:22:50.270 --> 1:22:52.510
--Leave Tot Musica to us!

1:22:52.510 --> 1:22:54.150
--So, please...!

1:22:54.150 --> 1:22:56.250
--Don't leave Uta-chan alone up there.

1:22:56.240 --> 1:22:57.430
--Go and finish it!

1:23:06.690 --> 1:23:09.730
Hey! I bet you can hear me now, Uta!

1:23:09.860 --> 1:23:11.110
This is all--

1:23:11.230 --> 1:23:12.230
Luffy-senpai!

1:23:16.360 --> 1:23:17.200
Luffy!

1:23:17.320 --> 1:23:18.990
What are you doing?! Fight back!

1:23:19.320 --> 1:23:21.620
Uta! Listen to me!

1:23:25.710 --> 1:23:27.460
Uta... we need to talk...

1:23:27.710 --> 1:23:31.500
I have nothing to say... to a pirate!

1:23:37.300 --> 1:23:37.970
Old guy!

1:23:38.090 --> 1:23:38.720
Bepo?!

1:23:38.840 --> 1:23:45.520
I cannot let Uta hurt any more of her friends...

1:23:45.640 --> 1:23:48.390
But this dummy still believes in Shanks.

1:23:48.520 --> 1:23:51.690
You're wrong, Uta. I lied...

1:23:51.980 --> 1:23:58.780
Twelve years ago... it wasn't the
Red-Haired Pirates who destroyed Elegia...

1:24:00.570 --> 1:24:02.070
It was Tot Musica!

1:24:03.830 --> 1:24:08.290
I'm sorry... that I never
told you the truth before.

1:24:09.290 --> 1:24:13.130
Do you remember the party from that day?

1:24:13.540 --> 1:24:18.010
When the musicians of the city learned,
you were leaving with Shanks,

1:24:18.130 --> 1:24:21.220
they realized it was their last-chance
and had you sing non-stop.

1:24:21.590 --> 1:24:28.730
and arranged it so that your singing
would play throughout the land.

1:24:29.480 --> 1:24:31.400
And that was a mistake.

1:24:33.270 --> 1:24:39.740
That singing beckoned to a score that
had been sealed deep under the castle!

1:24:47.160 --> 1:24:50.210
That score... was Tot Musica...

1:24:50.330 --> 1:24:54.380
It found its way to your side and tempted you

1:24:54.500 --> 1:24:58.300
so that it would be set free
with your Sing-Sing Fruit powers!

1:25:04.680 --> 1:25:09.020
With the seal on the Demon King
broken, he absorbed you,

1:25:09.140 --> 1:25:12.440
and unleashed his wrath on the country!

1:25:17.070 --> 1:25:20.150
Snap out of it, Uta!
Don't let him take you!

1:25:35.840 --> 1:25:38.750
Your youth ended up saving us.

1:25:38.880 --> 1:25:41.220
You were exhausted and fell asleep.

1:25:41.880 --> 1:25:44.430
But... the country was...

1:25:53.100 --> 1:25:55.350
The Navy is already here.

1:25:55.730 --> 1:25:58.270
Would you mind keeping this a secret from Uta?

1:25:58.440 --> 1:26:01.190
It'd be cruel to tell her the truth.

1:26:01.320 --> 1:26:04.950
Right. I'll tell the Navy
that I was responsible.

1:26:05.070 --> 1:26:07.240
Nah. It should be us.

1:26:07.780 --> 1:26:12.660
"Red-Haired" Shanks and his crew,
the Red-Haired Pirates, did this.

1:26:13.040 --> 1:26:14.460
Tell that to Uta, too.

1:26:16.080 --> 1:26:18.250
You're going to leave her...?

1:26:18.380 --> 1:26:20.840
The girl's got a hell of a voice.

1:26:20.960 --> 1:26:25.890
We can't keep her cooped up on a boat
while we're on the run from the Navy.

1:26:26.260 --> 1:26:30.350
Please. Make her into the
greatest singer in the world.

1:26:30.850 --> 1:26:33.600
Her singing isn't a crime.

1:26:33.890 --> 1:26:35.390
Shanks...

1:26:36.900 --> 1:26:38.270
I understand!

1:26:38.400 --> 1:26:44.070
As the king of Elegia, I, Gordon, swear upon
the love my subjects felt for music!

1:26:44.280 --> 1:26:50.280
I will turn Uta into a sublime singer,
who will spread joy to the entire world!

1:26:52.450 --> 1:26:59.540
Uta... even when we're apart,
you'll always be my daughter, so...

1:26:59.840 --> 1:27:05.300
Let's part with a smile!
Our beloved musician is setting off on her own!

1:27:09.470 --> 1:27:11.390
Uta! You heard him!

1:27:12.770 --> 1:27:14.270
I knew Shanks was a good guy!

1:27:33.160 --> 1:27:36.040
That's... my old drawing!

1:27:41.090 --> 1:27:43.750
It's done! Boom!

1:27:43.920 --> 1:27:45.010
What is it?

1:27:45.260 --> 1:27:47.340
It's Shanks' straw hat!

1:27:48.220 --> 1:27:49.180
A hat?

1:27:49.390 --> 1:27:50.390
Yeah!

1:27:52.300 --> 1:27:53.140
You suck.

1:27:53.260 --> 1:27:55.810
Let's make it the mark of our new age!

1:27:55.930 --> 1:27:57.730
You take that. Don't lose it!

1:28:00.770 --> 1:28:02.770
Stop, Uta.

1:28:03.980 --> 1:28:05.860
This isn't freedom.

1:28:07.320 --> 1:28:09.360
This isn't a new age!

1:28:10.820 --> 1:28:14.240
You know that better than anyone!

1:28:17.100 --> 1:28:17.960
Luffy--

1:28:19.620 --> 1:28:21.540
--Luffy!
--We're too late...

1:28:29.430 --> 1:28:31.470
What is this?

1:28:34.970 --> 1:28:37.560
Get in here if you want to be safe!

1:28:37.680 --> 1:28:40.520
Hey! How the hell are we
supposed to fight that thing?!

1:28:40.640 --> 1:28:43.860
If we just knew how to time
the simultaneous attacks...!

1:28:57.580 --> 1:29:00.910
Well, isn't that funny?

1:29:01.040 --> 1:29:06.130
The Navy's ready to kill civilians
and the pirates are protecting them.

1:29:06.250 --> 1:29:09.210
I don't think titles matter right now.

1:29:09.470 --> 1:29:11.590
Why protect them all?

1:29:11.720 --> 1:29:15.550
Because our daughter doesn't need
anything else on her conscience!

1:29:17.010 --> 1:29:19.980
All, right, you bozos!
Nobody else dies today!

1:29:22.390 --> 1:29:26.980
Stopping the Demon King might be faster...

1:29:29.820 --> 1:29:32.360
Uta's been eating Wake-shrooms.

1:29:32.490 --> 1:29:36.200
If she's been consumed by Tot Musica,
I'm not sure how she can be stopped...

1:29:37.910 --> 1:29:39.870
--Uta...
--You did it!
--It was your fault.

1:29:40.000 --> 1:29:41.870
--You did this!
--You're guilty...

1:29:42.000 --> 1:29:45.080
Shut up! I knew the truth!

1:29:46.000 --> 1:29:51.170
It happened a year after I started
singing for everyone...

1:29:51.470 --> 1:29:55.510
I found a Transponder Snail that recorded
what had happened on that day.

1:29:56.850 --> 1:29:59.600
If you're watching this, look out!

1:29:59.720 --> 1:30:01.560
The girl named Uta is dangerous!

1:30:01.680 --> 1:30:04.270
Her song can destroy the world!

1:30:04.810 --> 1:30:07.310
But what was I supposed to do at that point?!

1:30:07.440 --> 1:30:10.480
The whole world is waiting
for my singing already!

1:30:10.650 --> 1:30:13.740
Please, Uta. I don't want to be here anymore.

1:30:13.860 --> 1:30:18.200
Isn't there a world where I can just listen
to your singing all the time?

1:30:18.330 --> 1:30:21.580
That's right! I'm Uta and I hate pirates!

1:30:21.700 --> 1:30:24.290
For all the people who found me...

1:30:24.620 --> 1:30:26.920
I can't turn back anymore!

1:30:27.040 --> 1:30:28.250
For the new age--!

1:30:30.840 --> 1:30:32.670
Heat Goat!

1:30:38.350 --> 1:30:39.760
Big Brother Oven!

1:30:39.890 --> 1:30:40.850
Look out!

1:30:44.230 --> 1:30:46.980
Can't let a lady get hurt, can I?

1:30:47.980 --> 1:30:51.320
Besides, there's something
only you can do...

1:30:51.440 --> 1:30:52.320
Right!

1:30:53.940 --> 1:30:55.900
Koby, take command!

1:30:56.030 --> 1:30:58.240
Right! Defensive formation!

1:30:58.700 --> 1:31:00.830
Our main priority is protecting the audience!

1:31:00.950 --> 1:31:04.000
Nami-san, Robin-san
please help organize the evacuation!

1:31:04.330 --> 1:31:07.500
Ladies and gentlemen,
proceed calmly into the mirror!

1:31:07.620 --> 1:31:09.210
Brulee-san is at the center of this operation!

1:31:09.330 --> 1:31:11.500
Blueno-san, take your team and protect her!

1:31:11.920 --> 1:31:14.010
Franky-san, Jimbei-san, guard our flanks!

1:31:14.130 --> 1:31:17.590
Chopper-san, keep Luffy-san
and Gordon-san safe!

1:31:17.720 --> 1:31:20.220
Helmeppo-san and I will join flank guard!

1:31:20.350 --> 1:31:23.140
Usopp-san, provide fire support from the rear!

1:31:23.270 --> 1:31:26.560
Brook-san, Sanji-san,
you'll be frontline defense!

1:31:26.690 --> 1:31:31.690
Zoro-san will take point on attack,
along with Oven-san and Law-san!

1:31:31.820 --> 1:31:34.400
Let's get to work.

1:31:36.900 --> 1:31:41.160
Franky Rocket Launcher!

1:31:45.500 --> 1:31:47.330
Yummy, yummy, yummy!

1:31:47.710 --> 1:31:49.880
Yummy!

1:31:50.000 --> 1:31:52.750
Zeus! Breeze Tempo!

1:31:54.760 --> 1:31:55.880
Room!

1:31:57.670 --> 1:31:59.590
Uta! This is my fault!

1:31:59.720 --> 1:32:06.390
I was afraid of your power and missed
the chance to introduce you to the world!

1:32:06.520 --> 1:32:11.150
And... And as a music lover,

1:32:11.270 --> 1:32:14.610
I couldn't bring myself to throw
away the Tot Musica sheet!

1:32:14.730 --> 1:32:22.070
I'm a damned fool! A coward who
keeps making excuses to run away!

1:32:22.200 --> 1:32:23.910
I should be the only one who has to pay...

1:32:24.030 --> 1:32:28.330
Y'know, my old man always left me on my own!

1:32:28.620 --> 1:32:33.000
But you've been by Princess Uta's
side this whole time, right?

1:32:33.130 --> 1:32:35.800
Keeping your promise,
even after your country was wiped out.

1:32:35.920 --> 1:32:37.300
You're a heck of a guy!

1:32:42.220 --> 1:32:43.620
Okay, I'm going.

1:32:43.650 --> 1:32:44.300
Luffy?

1:32:44.430 --> 1:32:52.310
Luffy-kun! Her singing... it has the power
to bring joy to the entire world!

1:32:52.810 --> 1:32:57.030
For this to happen... it's just too tragic!

1:32:57.440 --> 1:33:04.660
Please, Luffy-kun! Save Uta!

1:33:07.490 --> 1:33:08.410
Luffy-san!

1:33:08.540 --> 1:33:12.170
Let him go! We're running out of time!

1:33:12.290 --> 1:33:14.960
If we can't do this, we're not
making it back to reality!

1:33:45.120 --> 1:33:46.490
Red-Haired!

1:33:46.830 --> 1:33:48.950
You need to attack simultaneously.

1:33:49.240 --> 1:33:53.670
At the same time and same point
as the attack in the Sing-Sing World.

1:33:55.710 --> 1:33:58.590
What's Big Mom's son doing here?

1:33:58.710 --> 1:34:01.800
I'm here to save my sister!

1:34:09.180 --> 1:34:14.270
Observation Haki lets me see the other side
through my sister's eyes for an instant.

1:34:14.390 --> 1:34:16.940
This thing is acting as a bridge between--

1:34:17.060 --> 1:34:18.400
I know!

1:34:19.190 --> 1:34:22.240
You're not the only one who
can use Observation Haki.

1:34:22.440 --> 1:34:25.610
Except my boy's got a long way to go!
He's too panicked!

1:34:25.780 --> 1:34:28.740
Still, I appreciate you showing up, Katakuri.

1:34:29.200 --> 1:34:32.040
The Navy seems to have their
hands full with the rescue.

1:34:34.620 --> 1:34:37.500
Don't suppose I can convince you to settle down?

1:34:49.260 --> 1:34:50.310
That must be Luffy.

1:34:50.680 --> 1:34:51.720
Shanks!

1:34:51.850 --> 1:34:52.610
That worked!

1:34:52.720 --> 1:34:54.770
We struck at the same time as in the real world!

1:35:04.740 --> 1:35:06.070
Did you just--?!

1:35:06.990 --> 1:35:09.030
Three-Swords Style Secret Art!

1:35:09.160 --> 1:35:10.700
Crossing the Six Paths!

1:35:13.290 --> 1:35:14.540
This isn't getting us anywhere.

1:35:15.120 --> 1:35:18.170
I can't believe that crap swordsman
used me for a boost!

1:35:18.290 --> 1:35:19.420
I'll get him for that!

1:35:20.590 --> 1:35:22.170
We don't have time for this!

1:35:25.760 --> 1:35:29.090
Dammit, if we could just do
something about its limbs!

1:35:30.390 --> 1:35:32.060
Get it together, Captain Usopp!

1:35:32.680 --> 1:35:34.850
In times like this, you gotta keep calm!

1:35:40.020 --> 1:35:40.440
Dad?!

1:35:40.560 --> 1:35:43.820
Finally noticed, you little knucklehead?

1:35:48.820 --> 1:35:51.870
I can see it! I can see what Dad sees!

1:35:52.410 --> 1:35:54.540
Luffy!

1:35:54.740 --> 1:35:59.880
All right, you guys! Give it all you've got!

1:36:00.000 --> 1:36:01.170
Yeah!

1:36:01.380 --> 1:36:05.300
All right, men... Give it all you've got!

1:36:05.420 --> 1:36:07.380
Yeah!

1:36:11.220 --> 1:36:13.220
We've gotta deal with Tot Musica's limbs!

1:36:13.720 --> 1:36:16.850
Take the shots as I call them!
Start with the right leg!

1:36:17.020 --> 1:36:18.020
Right leg!

1:36:34.160 --> 1:36:35.990
Left arm!

1:36:49.590 --> 1:36:51.010
Left leg!

1:36:51.260 --> 1:36:52.470
I guess we have to!

1:36:52.590 --> 1:36:54.970
You people owe me for this!

1:37:03.900 --> 1:37:05.400
Middle, on the right!

1:37:12.700 --> 1:37:13.870
Middle, on the left!

1:37:22.920 --> 1:37:26.000
Yasopp and his boy actually
get along pretty well.

1:37:26.130 --> 1:37:27.090
Right arm!

1:37:34.090 --> 1:37:37.970
Franky Fresh Fire!

1:37:48.280 --> 1:37:49.380
Luffy!

1:37:49.380 --> 1:37:50.170
Shanks!

1:37:50.320 --> 1:37:51.990
Go for it!

1:38:59.300 --> 1:39:02.220
Did you see that? They should've
never picked a fight with us!

1:39:02.350 --> 1:39:05.310
I'm glad they did!
This haul will keep us fed for a while!

1:39:05.440 --> 1:39:09.860
<i>Treasure for us, treasure for us,
treasure for us, treasure for us!</i>

1:39:15.240 --> 1:39:17.530
Where the heck did you come from?

1:39:17.660 --> 1:39:21.280
Did those pirates kidnap her from somewhere?

1:39:22.790 --> 1:39:23.910
You gotta be kidding me!

1:39:25.750 --> 1:39:28.080
Okay, you win! Quiet down! Uh...

1:39:28.750 --> 1:39:31.840
<i>Go to sleep, little baby...</i>

1:39:31.960 --> 1:39:33.920
<i>Nice and quiet-like!</i>

1:39:43.060 --> 1:39:45.480
Maybe this happened for a reason.

1:40:27.850 --> 1:40:31.440
What do you know...
I guess you were lonely, too.

1:40:39.450 --> 1:40:41.740
Shanks... I...

1:40:41.870 --> 1:40:44.080
It's fine! It's over now.

1:40:47.330 --> 1:40:50.290
If you drink this and sleep
right away, you'll make it.

1:40:50.750 --> 1:40:54.590
Shanks... I didn't wanna see you again.

1:40:55.500 --> 1:40:58.550
But... I missed you!

1:40:58.670 --> 1:41:01.300
Stop talking! Hurry and drink.

1:41:04.100 --> 1:41:05.470
What's going on here?!

1:41:05.600 --> 1:41:10.100
I thought beating the Demon King
would bring their souls back!

1:41:11.770 --> 1:41:12.940
Stop it...

1:41:13.650 --> 1:41:16.650
Stop fighting, please...

1:41:17.070 --> 1:41:18.400
Stop!

1:41:18.740 --> 1:41:21.320
Why aren't we back yet?! What's going on?!

1:41:21.450 --> 1:41:23.490
We were too late.

1:41:23.910 --> 1:41:28.950
Our souls were swallowed
by Tot Musica's power.

1:41:29.080 --> 1:41:30.370
No!

1:41:31.750 --> 1:41:34.420
Uta, hurry up and drink!

1:41:39.260 --> 1:41:43.300
I have to sing. I have to bring them all back.

1:41:45.800 --> 1:41:49.680
Shanks... remember what you told me?

1:41:50.350 --> 1:41:55.650
That my singing... has the power
to make people happy...

1:42:07.370 --> 1:42:13.040
I... I'm the musician of the Red-Haired Pirates, Uta!

1:42:50.080 --> 1:43:02.630
<i>♪I recall that day
we played together by the sea,
just you and me</i>♪

1:43:03.630 --> 1:43:16.600
<i>♪Still that scent of ocean
seems to fade each passing day♪</i>

1:43:13.340 --> 1:43:16.590
<i>♪It slips away♪</i>

1:43:16.730 --> 1:43:23.230
<i>♪So I sing an old familar song
I hope you know the one♪</i>

1:43:23.360 --> 1:43:29.820
<i>♪I will sing to call you back to me♪</i>

1:43:31.030 --> 1:43:37.040
<i>♪I need you to hear it
Need you to believe in♪</i>

1:43:37.170 --> 1:43:44.210
<i>♪Something out there beyond the open sea
Out in the starlight♪</i>

1:43:44.340 --> 1:43:50.760
<i>♪I need you to hear it
Need you to believe in♪</i>

1:43:50.890 --> 1:43:56.430
<i>♪There's a wind stirring my wings
That is always beckoning♪</i>

1:43:56.810 --> 1:44:05.530
<i>♪Calling me above into the open sky♪</i>

1:44:09.160 --> 1:44:13.280
The singing voice of an angel... That's Uta.

1:44:13.410 --> 1:44:19.170
<i>♪Tried my best to hear it
Trying to believe in♪</i>

1:44:19.290 --> 1:44:25.880
<i>♪Something out there beyond the open sea
Out in the starlight♪</i>

1:44:26.010 --> 1:44:31.720
<i>♪Trying to believe it
I think I believe it♪</i>

1:44:31.840 --> 1:44:38.100
<i>♪That one day we'll meet again
And continue this dreamland♪</i>

1:44:38.230 --> 1:44:50.410
<i>♪In the gleaming dawn
we'll wake up once again♪</i>

1:45:17.560 --> 1:45:21.230
Hey, how come you didn't actually hit me?

1:45:21.940 --> 1:45:25.400
Didn't I tell you? My punches
hit harder than a pistol.

1:45:25.520 --> 1:45:28.900
You used to do it all the time, though.
Those wimpy, spinny punches of yours!

1:45:29.030 --> 1:45:30.530
Those weren't for real!

1:45:32.110 --> 1:45:34.700
You're being a sore loser again!

1:45:38.040 --> 1:45:41.960
I guess you got taller than me
at some point, huh?

1:45:54.090 --> 1:45:56.930
This hat means a lot to me, too.

1:45:58.890 --> 1:46:03.230
I want you to be a man who's even
more worthy of it someday, okay?

1:46:11.650 --> 1:46:15.070
Shanks... Is Luffy...?

1:46:15.200 --> 1:46:16.620
He's back.

1:46:16.910 --> 1:46:18.450
The entire audience, too.

1:46:22.290 --> 1:46:23.290
What a relief...

1:46:25.830 --> 1:46:31.760
Sorry. I should've believed in you
and the Red-Haired Pirates.

1:46:33.800 --> 1:46:38.470
But... you still came to help me. Thank you.

1:46:42.680 --> 1:46:45.650
Now then, how about you hand Uta,

1:46:45.770 --> 1:46:50.690
the arch criminal who almost
destroyed the world, over to us?

1:46:53.890 --> 1:46:55.490
You people...

1:46:55.610 --> 1:46:59.240
I take it you won't cooperate, then?

1:47:00.330 --> 1:47:01.740
Everyone...

1:47:02.120 --> 1:47:03.450
This girl...

1:47:04.210 --> 1:47:05.290
is my daughter.

1:47:07.080 --> 1:47:09.840
She's a precious part of our family.

1:47:10.880 --> 1:47:13.380
If you wanna take her...

1:47:13.800 --> 1:47:15.470
...you'd better be ready to die!

1:47:22.600 --> 1:47:26.060
That even took down a handful of vice admirals.

1:47:26.190 --> 1:47:29.770
So this is Haki of Shanks,
one of the four Emperors...

1:47:30.980 --> 1:47:32.940
Let's stand down.

1:47:33.110 --> 1:47:38.160
I'd rather not go to war with
so many civilians around.

1:47:57.300 --> 1:48:01.100
Are my fans gonna be okay?

1:48:01.720 --> 1:48:05.470
They'll be fine. People aren't that fragile.

1:48:05.730 --> 1:48:09.060
Besides... a new age is dawning soon.

1:48:15.990 --> 1:48:23.330
<i>♪Where did it come from?
Where could this wind be taking us?</i>♪

1:48:24.330 --> 1:48:31.130
<i>♪I look up to the sky hoping for answers
But there is no reply</i>♪

1:48:31.830 --> 1:48:39.970
<i>♪Where will it end up,
This song that I've been a vessel for?</i>♪

1:48:40.470 --> 1:48:47.640
<i>♪I look within knowing I'll find the answer
Even on my own</i>♪

1:48:49.690 --> 1:48:55.690
<i>♪Let's row out to the open sea,
far as we can go</i>♪

1:48:56.860 --> 1:48:59.070
<i>♪To the unknown</i>♪

1:49:02.780 --> 1:49:08.040
<i>♪I've got to keep on dreamin'</i>♪

1:49:08.870 --> 1:49:15.460
<i>♪No surrenderin'
Go on</i>♪

1:49:16.250 --> 1:49:26.930
<i>♪Hoist the sail inside my open heart
And let me heed the call of the sea</i>♪

1:49:27.390 --> 1:49:32.810
<i>♪I've got to keep on singin'...</i>♪

1:49:36.870 --> 1:49:38.510
You were asleep for a while.

1:49:39.490 --> 1:49:41.450
Where's Uta? And Shanks?

1:49:41.570 --> 1:49:42.490
There.

1:50:22.030 --> 1:50:28.870
<i>♪Where did it come from?
Where could this wind be taking us?♪</i>

1:50:29.370 --> 1:50:35.330
<i>♪I look up to the sky hoping for answers
But there is no reply♪</i>

1:50:35.750 --> 1:50:42.920
♪Where will it end up,
This song I've been a vessel for?♪

1:50:43.050 --> 1:50:49.010
<i>♪I look within knowing I'll find the answer
Even on my own</i>♪

1:50:49.890 --> 1:50:55.520
<i>♪Let's row out to the open sea,
Far as we can go</i>♪

1:50:56.350 --> 1:50:59.190
<i> ♪To the unknown...</i>♪

1:51:01.440 --> 1:51:06.030
<i>♪I've got to keep on dreamin'</i>♪

1:51:06.570 --> 1:51:12.410
<i>♪No surrenderin'
Go on</i>♪

1:51:13.040 --> 1:51:21.840
<i>♪Hoist the sail inside my open heart
